window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1 Serpent’s Coil","paragraphs":["The main screen flashed green.","SUCCESS","For one stunned second, the clean room went silent.","Then the lab exploded.","\"We got it!\"","Cheers broke out across the room. Someone slapped Eira on the shoulder as Professor Davies pushed through the crowd and pulled her into a quick hug.","\"Eira, look at those numbers. This is huge. We just changed the game.\"","A researcher behind him let out a low whistle. \"National pride, military contracts, and enough money to make half the country lose its mind. Not bad for one night, Dr. Crawford.\"","Davies leaned closer so she could hear him over the noise.","\"Your husband is Alpha Sebastian Hale, right?\"","Eira nodded.","\"This could give Hale Pack a serious edge,\" he said. \"If they get access before the other Packs, they’ll leave everyone else in the dust.\"","His words hit harder than she expected.","She pictured Sebastian opening the certification report. His face would go still first. Then his eyes would sharpen. Maybe, just maybe, he would look at her with something close to respect.","She had wanted that look for four years.","\"I’ll tell him tonight,\" Eira said.","Davies grinned. \"Good. Let him see what you’ve been up to.\"","Eira smiled, but her fingers tightened around the folder.","[No, ]she thought.","[I’m giving him the biggest advantage of his life because I’m his wife.]","She cleared three security checkpoints, changed out of her clean-room suit, and collected the final certification documents.","Her name was printed across the first page.","Dr. Eira Crawford.","She ran her thumb over the title.","This time, no one could call her useless. No one could brush her off as a wolfless omega. No one could say she had nothing to offer an Alpha.","She had built something powerful enough to make entire Packs fight for access.","And tonight, she was going to put it in Sebastian Hale’s hands.","--","The VIP elevator took her straight to the top floor of Hale Tower an hour later. Alpha Sebastian used the private suite for late business meetings, and sometimes he slept there when he claimed Hale Group’s work ran too late. Eira had brought him dinner there more times than she could count.","This time she brought him a future.","She stepped out of the elevator with the folder held against her chest. The hallway was quiet, thick with expensive carpet and soft yellow wall lights. She was twenty feet from his office when her steps slowed.","Her nose knew before her mind did.","Cedar. Sharp, familiar, warm in the way only Alpha Sebastian’s scent could be. It was the scent she had fallen asleep beside for four years, even when his side of the bed stayed cold too long.","But under it was something else.","Sweet. Floral. Not hers.","Eira stopped.","The office door was not fully closed. A thin line of light spilled through the gap, and with it came the mixed scents of two people standing too close.","Then Alpha Sebastian spoke.","\"Serena, you know I’ve always loved you. She means nothing.\"","The folder slipped slightly in Eira’s grip. She caught it before it fell.","Serena’s voice came next, soft and wet around the edges, but there was a thin blade of amusement underneath. \"If you love me, why did you let that Omega orphan become your Luna? Why didn’t you come after me when I left?\"","Alpha Sebastian gave a low laugh. Eira knew that laugh. He used it when he wanted someone to feel foolish for doubting him. \"You’re jealous?\"","\"Shouldn’t I be?\" Serena asked.","\"I chose her because you left,\" Alpha Sebastian said. His voice softened, but the softness made it worse. \"I needed a Luna. The elders wanted the position filled, and Eira was harmless. No family. No wolf. No one to challenge me.\"","Harmless.","Eira stood outside the door, unable to breathe.","Serena made a small sound of disgust. \"And now?\"","\"Now she’s useful.\" Alpha Sebastian sounded almost bored. \"She runs the house, handles Pack accounts, keeps my mother from turning every dinner into a war. Why would I throw away a tool that still works?\"","The word sank into Eira slowly.","Tool.","Not wife. Not Luna. Not partner.","Tool.","Serena was silent for a moment. When she spoke again, her voice had lost its tears. \"I don’t want to stay hidden forever.\"","\"You won’t.\" Fabric shifted inside the room. \"When the time is right, the Luna position will be yours.\"","\"And the heir?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s answer came without hesitation. \"My heir will only come from you.\"","Eira closed her eyes.","For four years, Alpha Sebastian had avoided touching her. He told her she was young. He told her the silver poisoning he suffered years ago might still affect his body. He said he did not want to hurt her. She had believed him because she wanted to believe there was kindness inside the distance. She had thought he respected her. She had thought patience was love wearing a quiet face.","No.","The truth was simple.","She was not Serena.","Through the crack in the door, she saw Alpha Sebastian lower his head to Serena’s neck. His nose brushed her skin, and his expression changed in a way Eira had never seen directed at her. Desire made his proud face almost drunk.","\"I missed you,\" he murmured. \"Your scent. Your voice.\"","Serena leaned into him. \"Then divorce her.\"","\"Not yet.\"","\"Why?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s tone cooled, turning into the voice he used in board meetings. \"Because she still serves a purpose. Give her a little attention, and she’ll do anything for this family. Don’t touch the tool before I’m done using it.\"","Eira’s fingers tightened around the folder until the edge bent.","Inside it was a certification that could have changed Hale Pack’s future. She had imagined placing it on Alpha Sebastian’s desk and watching pride finally dawn in his eyes. She had imagined him saying her name like it mattered.","Instead, she heard the truth.","For a moment, pain emptied her completely. Then something colder moved in.","She took out her phone with steady hands and pressed record. The screen captured the gap in the door, the angle of Alpha Sebastian’s face, Serena’s hands on his shirt, the kiss that followed, the way he whispered her name like a vow. Eira recorded until her soul felt far away from her body. Five minutes. Enough for any lawyer. Enough for any Council hearing. Enough for any fool who later tried to call her dramatic.","Then she stopped the recording.","She walked back to the elevator without making a sound. The doors closed around her, cutting off cedar and flowers at last.","In the polished steel, her reflection looked calm.","So calm it felt like a stranger was staring back.","***","Outside Hale Tower, the cold air hit Eira’s face. She did not cry. Tears felt too small for what had happened.","She called the legal division of the National Research Institute. Susan answered on the third ring.","\"Dr. Crawford?\"","\"I need a formal mate separation agreement. I have proof of my mate’s affair. I want the bond ended and my name removed from all Hale Pack records as soon as possible.\"","\"Standard filing or protected status?\"","\"Full protection. Highest level. Sebastian must not learn about my security clearance.\"","Susan paused. \"That process will cost you.\"","\"I don’t care how much it costs.\" Eira looked up at Hale Tower. \"Get his signature before he figures out what he’s losing.\"","She ended the call and walked away without looking back."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2 The Silk Thread Pulled Loose","paragraphs":["By morning, the city looked ordinary again.","That felt almost insulting.","Cars moved through intersections. Office workers bought coffee. A woman in a red coat laughed into her phone as if the world had not split open the night before.","Eira sat in the back of a taxi with her black folder on her knees and watched sunlight slide over Hale Tower’s glass walls.","The building still stood. The sky had not cracked. Alpha Sebastian Hale had not been struck by lightning for calling his wife a tool.","Apparently betrayal did not disturb public infrastructure.","At eight sharp, Susan’s email arrived. The subject line was simple: Formal Mate Separation Agreement — Confidential Draft.","Eira opened it on her phone and read the first page without blinking.","The language was clean, bloodless, and almost elegant in its cruelty.","Termination of spousal obligations.","Withdrawal of Luna status from Hale Pack records. Separation of assets. Severance of domestic authority. No future duty of care.","Four years of marriage, translated into clauses and signature lines.","Good, Eira thought.","Feelings had made her weak. Paper would make her free.","She asked for a day off from the lab, then went back to the apartment she had shared with Alpha Sebastian for four years.","Calling it home suddenly felt like lying.","The place was quiet when she entered, the kind of quiet expensive buildings sold as luxury.","The refrigerator hummed. Sunlight fell across the living room floor. A pair of Alpha Sebastian’s shoes stood by the entrance, polished and arrogant.","Eira looked at them for one second too long, then walked past.","Packing took less time than it should have.","Her clothes occupied less than half of one closet. The rest belonged to Alpha Sebastian: suits arranged by color, shirts folded with military precision, watches in velvet boxes, ties he had worn to dinners where she sat beside him and pretended not to hear his relatives whisper.","Eira took out her own dresses, jeans, lab blouses, and the few sweaters she had bought with her own salary. She folded each piece carefully and placed them into cardboard boxes.","In the bathroom, her face cream and toothbrush were pushed into a corner. Alpha Sebastian’s expensive grooming bottles took up most of the counter. She packed her small things into a toiletry bag and almost laughed.","Four years, and her life fit into two boxes and one suitcase.","The delivery service confirmed pickup for the afternoon. The boxes would go to her small apartment on the other side of the city, the one she had bought with her first year’s pay from the Research Institute before she married Alpha Sebastian. Thirty-five square meters. Old heating. Bad view. Hers.","The word felt strange.","Hers.","She showered after the movers left. Hot water beat against the back of her neck until her skin turned pink, but it could not wash away the memory of cedar mixed with flowers. When she stepped out, she put on a thin slip dress because most of her clothes were already gone. Her hair dripped down her shoulders as she plugged in the hairdryer.","The front door opened.","Eira saw Alpha Sebastian in the mirror before she turned. He stopped at the bedroom entrance, one hand still on the doorframe. He wore a dark suit, his tie loosened, his expression unreadable. His gaze moved over the suitcase near the wall, then over her wet hair, bare shoulders, and the hem of her dress.","\"Eira.\"","He said her name low, almost carefully.","She picked up the hairdryer and turned it on. Warm air roared between them. The sound filled the room, simple and mechanical. Safe.","He did not like being ignored. She saw that in the mirror. His jaw tightened first, then his eyes grew cold. Still, he came closer. The scent of cedar followed him, and beneath it she thought she caught the faintest trace of floral sweetness. Maybe it was real. Maybe her mind was cruel enough to invent it.","His hand reached around her waist.","The hairdryer stopped. He had pulled the plug from the wall.","Eira went very still.","Alpha Sebastian leaned down as if to kiss her. She turned her head at the last second, and his mouth landed near her ear instead of her lips.","Silence dropped heavily into the room.","\"You’re avoiding me?\" he asked.","She met his eyes in the mirror. \"Yes.\"","For a moment, he looked genuinely confused. In four years, she had never said that word to him in that tone. She had adjusted. Smoothed things over. Made excuses. Loved quietly enough not to bother him.","His fingers closed around her chin, turning her face toward him. \"You were the one who wanted me to touch you before.\"","Her fingertips curled against the counter. \"Before was before.\"","\"And now?\" His voice sharpened. \"Now I touch you once, and you dodge?\"","She said nothing.","His expression changed. Suspicion entered his eyes, ugly and fast. \"Is there someone else?\"","Eira stared at him.","He had returned to their marriage carrying another woman’s scent. He had called her harmless, useful, a tool. He had promised his heir to Serena. Yet his first thought was that Eira had betrayed him.","The unfairness was so complete it almost became funny.","\"That question,\" she said, \"is not yours to ask me.\"","The last trace of patience disappeared from Alpha Sebastian’s face. His Alpha scent surged, cedar turning sharp and heavy. It filled the room like an invisible net, pushing against her lungs, demanding obedience from instincts she did not have. A wolfless body could still feel Alpha pressure, but it did not bow the same way. There was no wolf inside her to roll over.","So Eira only looked at him.","That seemed to provoke him more than screaming would have.","\"Don’t use that tone with me.\"","Before she could step back, he grabbed her wrist and dragged her toward the bedroom.","\"Sebastian—\"","The door hit the wall with a dull crack. He pushed her onto the bed and came down over her. This was not love. It was not regret. It was not a husband finally reaching for his wife after years of restraint.","It was possession trying to prove it still owned what was walking away.","Panic flashed white behind Eira’s eyes, but rage came faster. She bent her knee and kicked upward with all the strength in her body. Alpha Sebastian grunted, his grip loosening for half a breath. She twisted free, pushed herself up, and slapped him across the face.","Crack.","The sound was bright and clean.","His head turned with the force of it.","For one second, neither of them moved.","Then his hand swung back.","Pain exploded across her cheek. Her head snapped to the side, and iron filled her mouth. The room tilted. She did not cry out, but tears spilled anyway, hot and humiliating.","Alpha Sebastian froze as if the sight of her tears had finally reached a part of him that his own violence had not.","\"Eira, I—\"","She did not let him finish.","She grabbed the blanket from the foot of the bed, wrapped it around herself, snatched up her phone and ID, and walked out barefoot. His voice followed her once, then stopped. Maybe pride held him back. Maybe guilt did. Maybe he simply could not imagine she would actually leave.","The elevator doors closed before he decided.","Eira walked ten minutes through the cold evening streets. Her feet stung against the pavement. A man outside a convenience store stared at the blanket around her shoulders and the red mark on her face. She kept walking. If she lowered her head, she would cry harder, and she refused to give strangers that much of herself.","A hotel appeared on the corner, silver-gray and bright against the dark street.","Sterling Hotel.","She knew the name. Everyone did. Sterling Group owned hotels, resorts, and half the luxury properties powerful Packs used when they wanted to pretend business meetings were vacations.","Eira stepped into the lobby.","The front desk clerk looked up. His eyes moved over her wet hair, blanket, bare feet, and swollen cheek. To his credit, he did not ask the wrong questions.","\"One room,\" Eira said. Her voice sounded rough. \"One night.\"","He checked her in quickly. \"Room 1806. The elevator is on your right. If you need medical assistance or security, dial zero.\"","\"Thank you.\"","She took the key card and walked to the elevator. The doors were almost closed when a hand stopped them.","They opened again.","A man stood outside.","Tall. Dark shirt with the sleeves rolled up. Black hair, calm posture, and eyes the color of a frozen lake. His gaze touched her face, her wrists, her bare feet. He saw everything. He did not stare long enough to make it worse.","He stepped inside and stood beside her, leaving more space than the elevator required.","His scent was controlled, but the small space carried a trace of it to her anyway. Mint. Cold. Clean. Like leaves crushed in ice.","The elevator did not move. Eira realized she had not pressed a floor.","\"Which floor?\" he asked.","\"Eighteenth.\"","He swiped a black card, then pressed the button. The elevator rose smoothly.","Eira held her key card tightly. Her cheek throbbed. The stranger did not ask who had hit her. He did not offer pity. He did not crowd her with his body or his scent. He simply stood there, still as stone, and somehow the silence felt less dangerous than any comfort Alpha Sebastian had ever given her.","Ding.","The eighteenth floor opened. Eira stepped out. \"Thank you.\"","\"You’re welcome.\"","She did not look back.","In room 1806, she locked the door, put the chain on, and stood there until her breathing slowed. The room was clean and anonymous: white bed, gray curtains, desk, lamp, bottled water she had not paid for yet. No cedar. No floral scent. No shoes by the door.","She sat on the edge of the bed and pressed her palm against her bruised cheek.","Then the doorbell rang.","Eira went still.","If Alpha Sebastian had found her, she would not run this time.","Her eyes moved to the glass water bottle on the desk. Slowly, she picked it up by the neck and walked toward the door."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3 The Sterling Wolf","paragraphs":["Killian Sterling built half his reputation on showing up when nobody expected him. Announced visits were useless—staff smiled harder, managers hid problems. If he wanted the truth, he came with no warning and no patience.","That’s why he stood in the Sterling Hotel lobby at nine-thirty on a weeknight, half-listening to Miles read off complaint numbers while the manager behind the desk sweated through his shirt.","\"Noise complaints are up on sixteen and seventeen,\" Miles said. \"Two guest-care issues from last month never got closed.\"","Alpha Killian raised one hand. Miles stopped talking.","Across the lobby, a woman was checking in. No shoes. Wet hair stuck to her neck. A red handprint on her cheek. Marks circled both wrists, too clean to be an accident.","She looked tired enough to see through. But she stood straight.","Not the kind of pride a Pack daughter wore like jewelry. Something quieter.","Someone holding herself together by force.","Inside Alpha Killian, Rowan stirred.","The silver-gray wolf had slept through most of the evening’s business reports with his usual contempt. Now he rose so fast Alpha Killian’s muscles tightened.","[Follow her, ] Rowan said.","[No, ] Alpha Killian answered.","[Find out who hurt her.]","[Not here.]","The woman took her key card and moved toward the elevator. Her steps were steady, but her toes were white from the cold floor. The elevator doors began to close.","Alpha Killian moved before he had decided to.","His hand caught the doors. They opened, and she looked up.","Blue eyes. Bloodshot. Empty in a way that made something in his chest contract.","Alpha Killian knew fear. He had seen it in traitors dragged before Pack judgment, in businessmen realizing they had signed the wrong contract, in rival Alphas when Rowan showed his teeth. This was not fear. Not exactly. It was the look of someone who had already been hurt and had no room left to be surprised.","He stepped into the elevator and stood beside her, careful to leave space. Rowan hated the distance. Alpha Killian kept it anyway.","The elevator waited. She had not pressed a floor.","\"Which floor?\" he asked.","\"Eighteenth.\"","Her voice was rough, but she did not lower her eyes. He swiped his black card and pressed the button. The elevator rose. Her scent reached him in fragments under soap, rain, and pain. Not perfume. Not practiced sweetness. Something clean, faint, and warm beneath the cold.","Rowan went utterly still.","Not with lust. With recognition.","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened. He did not move closer. He did not ask questions. A wounded woman did not need an Alpha filling a steel box with demands, even if every instinct in him wanted to turn the building upside down until someone named the person who had left those marks on her skin.","The doors opened on eighteen. She stepped out and thanked him without looking back.","Alpha Killian watched until the hallway swallowed her.","\"Alpha?\" Miles’s voice came through the phone in his ear. \"Should I continue the report?\"","\"No.\" Alpha Killian looked at the number glowing above the elevator. \"Put a welfare note on the female guest who just checked in. No one gives out her room number. If anyone asks for her, security informs me before answering. If she calls the front desk, she gets priority.\"","A short pause. \"Yes, Alpha.\"","\"And send slippers, anti-swelling cream, and water to her.\"","\"Of course.\" Another pause, more careful this time. \"Do you want staff to deliver them?\"","Alpha Killian looked at his own reflection in the elevator’s polished wall. Cold eyes. Still face. The same face that had made Council elders sit straighter for eight years.","He should let staff deliver them.","Rowan’s growl rolled through him, low and furious.","\"Bring them to me,\" Alpha Killian said.","There were reasons people called him the Sterling Wolf. Some were exaggerated. Most were not.","At twenty, he had taken Sterling Pack from his father after a family challenge no one outside the inner circle still dared discuss.","Half the old Alphas expected him to fail.","Two years later, a high-ranking traitor sold border routes to rogues and tried to murder three patrol guards in their sleep. Alpha Killian did not ask the Council for permission to act.","The next morning, the Council received a video of a silver-gray wolf standing over the traitor’s body at the edge of Sterling territory. The message had been simple: Sterling law protects Sterling blood.","No one called him a child after that.","They called him dangerous. They called him ambitious. They called him unmated like it was a disease waiting to spread.","At twenty-eight, Alpha Killian ran nine hotels, three resorts, and the most disciplined Pack in the northern region.","Council elders had begun sending him daughters wrapped in silk and political convenience. He had not wanted any of them.","Want was a messy word. Alpha Killian preferred control.","Then a barefoot stranger with bruises on her wrists stepped into his hotel, and control suddenly felt like a thin leash in his fist.","Miles brought the bag himself. He did not ask questions. Smart man.","Alpha Killian took the paper bag to room 1806 and knocked once. Inside, silence. Then soft movement. He saw the shadow shift behind the peephole.","\"Good evening, Miss Crawford,\" he said, reading the name the front desk had recorded on the welfare note and nothing more. \"Sterling Hotel provides basic guest care for visible injuries. You may refuse it.\"","A pause.","The door opened only a crack. The chain remained in place.","Good, Alpha Killian thought. She had sense.","Her blue eyes moved from his face to the bag. In her right hand, half hidden by the door, she held a glass bottle by the neck.","The corner of Alpha Killian’s mouth almost moved. \"Also a good choice. Aim for the temple if you need to.\"","For the first time, something like life flickered in her eyes. Not amusement exactly. More like disbelief that he had said that.","\"I’ll remember,\" she said.","He held up the bag. \"Slippers. Cream. Water. No charge. No conversation required.\"","\"That sounds like conversation.\"","\"Then I’ll make it short.\"","After another moment, she slid the chain free and opened the door enough to take the bag. Her fingers brushed the back of his hand. Ice cold. Alpha Killian’s wolf surged toward the contact. Alpha Killian held him back so hard pain flashed behind his eyes.","\"Thank you,\" she said.","His gaze dropped to the bruises on her wrists before he could stop it. The marks were shaped by fingers. Too large to be hers.","\"Your face,\" he said carefully, \"and your wrists. Do you need security or medical help?\"","Her expression closed at once. \"I had a fight with my husband.\"","\"A fight,\" Alpha Killian repeated.","Her mouth curved slightly, but there was no humor in it. \"That is the polite version.\"","\"The polite version usually lies.\"","She looked at him then, really looked. Most people looked away when Alpha Killian’s attention landed fully on them. Eira Crawford did not. Exhausted, hurt, wrapped in a blanket, she still held his gaze as if she had already survived something worse than him tonight.","\"I’m handling it,\" she said.","He believed her. He also believed that handling something alone did not mean a person should have to.","\"You should consider finding a good lawyer.\" The words came out sharper than he had intended.","A tiny shift crossed her face. Not surprise. Recognition. \"Thank you for the advice. I already have one.\"","Of course she did.","Alpha Killian inclined his head. \"Then I hope they’re ruthless.\"","This time, the ghost of something almost like a smile touched her mouth. \"She is.\"","The door began to close.","\"Miss Crawford.\"","She paused.","\"No one gets your room number from my staff. If anyone bothers you, call zero.\"","For a heartbeat, the guarded look in her eyes softened.","\"Good night,\" she said.","The door closed. The lock clicked. Then the chain slid back into place.","Alpha Killian stood in the hallway for longer than necessary. Behind that door was a married woman with bruises, a lawyer, and eyes too empty for her age. None of that was his business.","Rowan disagreed.","Mine, the wolf said.","Alpha Killian’s hand tightened around nothing.","No, he told the wolf. Not unless she chooses.","The answer did not calm either of them.","When the elevator arrived, Alpha Killian stepped inside and pressed the button for the top floor instead of the lobby. Miles called again before the doors fully closed.","\"Alpha, are we continuing the inspection?\"","\"Temporary schedule change,\" Alpha Killian said. His voice had returned to its usual coldness. \"I’m staying at Sterling Hotel for a few days.\"","\"For the guest complaints?\" Miles asked, far too carefully.","Alpha Killian looked at the glowing number eighteen as the elevator rose past it.","\"For now.\""]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4 Dinner Invitation","paragraphs":["The next morning, Eira woke before her alarm.","For a few seconds, she did not know where she was. The ceiling was white instead of cream. The bed smelled like hotel detergent instead of cedar. Her cheek throbbed when she moved, and memory returned with the dull efficiency of a knife being placed on a table.","Alpha Sebastian. Serena.","Then the slap.","Eira sat up slowly. The slippers from the paper bag waited beside the bed. She had put them there before sleeping, because the floor was cold and because practical kindness was harder to reject than pity. The anti-swelling cream sat on the nightstand. Her cheek was still marked, but the redness had gone down.","Her laptop showed three unread emails from Susan.","The final agreement was ready.","Eira read it twice, then a third time. Every clause had a purpose. The first page looked harmless enough: Pack operational authority update, monthly finance approval, domestic account restructuring.","Alpha Sebastian had signed dozens of documents like it before without reading beyond the title. The true separation terms began on page four, shielded beneath language he would consider boring.","Eira did not feel guilty.","Alpha Sebastian read contracts when he respected the person across the table. He checked clauses when he feared betrayal. With rivals, board members, suppliers, and Council lawyers, he was careful to the point of arrogance.","With her, he signed.","Because you do not check the blade in a tool’s hand.","She returned to the apartment before noon to change. Alpha Sebastian was leaving when she stepped out of the elevator. He stopped immediately.","He looked perfect. Dark suit. Clean shave. Hair neat. No sign of the man who had lost control the night before, except for the faint red mark on his cheek where her hand had landed.","His eyes moved to her face, and regret appeared. Not enough to be useful. Just enough to insult her.","\"Eira,\" he said softly, the way people spoke to frightened animals. \"Last night was my fault. I drank too much. My head wasn’t clear.\"","\"Drank too much,\" she repeated. \"But your hands seemed very clear.\"","His expression stiffened. Then he covered it with the warm public smile that had fooled half the Pack. \"I was wrong.\"","He took a small box from inside his jacket and opened it. A silk scarf lay inside, pale gold with a designer logo printed near the edge.","Even at a glance, the thing wasn’t cheap—funny, for a man who always claimed the Pack was running on empty. Guess there was still room in the budget when it came to an apology.","\"This is for you,\" he said. \"My apology.\"","Eira looked at the scarf. Yesterday, she would have wondered if this meant he cared. Today, she wondered whether Serena’s gift had come in a larger box.","\"No need,\" she said. \"I think someone else deserves it more.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s smile faltered.","For one second, calculation moved behind his eyes. Did she know? How much did she know? Then pride came to rescue him, as it always did. He decided she could not possibly know anything dangerous.","He closed the box. \"By the way, tonight is the Pack’s monthly family dinner. You still need to come.\"","Need.","There it was. Not please. Not would you. Need.","Every last Friday of the month, the core Hale family and senior Pack members gathered at the main house. For four years, Eira had handled everything: menus, seating, wine, elders’ allergies, Margaret’s temper, Isabella’s sudden requests, Alpha Sebastian’s preference for low-salt food after late meetings. She had cooked when the chef was sick, cleaned emotional messes when family fights broke out, and made sure everyone left full enough to still insult her comfortably.","Tonight, she had no intention of feeding anyone.","But she did have a reason to go.","The agreement sat in her bag, printed and clipped beneath the routine finance approval forms. Alpha Sebastian would be relaxed after dinner. His family would be present, Serena possibly too. If he signed in front of them without reading, it would be almost poetic.","Eira lifted her eyes. \"I’ll be there.\"","Alpha Sebastian seemed relieved. That almost made her laugh. He thought obedience had returned because she had answered calmly.","At seven that evening, Eira drove into the Hale family driveway. The main house glowed with porch lights. Through the open windows came Margaret’s voice, loud enough for the flowers outside to suffer.","\"That worthless mixed-blood girl is late again. Always running off as if she has something important to do.\"","Isabella’s bored voice followed. \"She probably has office papers to staple. Very demanding career.\"","Eira opened the front door and walked in.","Three faces turned toward her. Margaret sat at the head of the living room sofa like a queen without a country. Isabella lounged with her phone in hand. Alpha Roger emerged from the study, already frowning.","\"I’m here,\" Eira said, setting down her bag. \"Please continue. I’d hate to interrupt quality family education.\"","No one spoke for a beat.","Margaret recovered first. \"Dinner needs to be made. The kitchen is waiting.\"","\"There’s a chef for that.\"","\"The chef has the night off. You know Friday dinners are your responsibility.\"","\"No,\" Eira said. \"They were my habit. I’m breaking it.\"","Margaret stared at her as if the furniture had started talking back. \"What did you say?\"","Eira took out her phone and opened a delivery app. \"I said I’m not cooking. If you want food, order it. I recommend poached shrimp, garlic broccoli, low salt, low oil. Very tragic, but survivable.\"","Isabella lowered her phone. \"Are you insane?\"","\"No. Hungry.\"","\"You’re a wolfless Omega,\" Isabella snapped. \"If you can’t even cook, what can you do? My brother gave you the Luna title. Without him, no Pack would even look at you.\"","Four years ago, those words would have sent Eira into the kitchen with a polite smile and burning eyes. Tonight, she felt only a clean coldness.","\"Your words smell bad,\" she said. \"If you want dinner, make it yourself. Don’t expect me to spoon-feed you.\"","Margaret rose so fast her necklace jumped against her throat. \"Who do you think you are?\" She seized Eira’s wrist, nails biting into skin. \"No family, no wolf, no power. My son marrying you was a gift, and you dare speak to me like this in my own house?\"","Eira looked down at the hand on her wrist.","Last night, Alpha Sebastian’s fingers had left bruises there. Margaret’s nails pressed close to them now.","Something inside Eira clicked into place.","She closed her hand around Margaret’s wrist and tightened just enough.","Margaret gasped. Shock spread across her face. She had expected tears, apologies, retreat. Not resistance.","\"Let go,\" Eira said. \"If you don’t, I’ll show everyone here that being wolfless doesn’t mean being weak.\"","\"You wouldn’t dare—\"","\"One.\"","\"This is my home.\"","\"Two.\"","Margaret jerked her hand free before Eira reached three. She stumbled back and hit a chair with a dull thud. Isabella’s mouth fell open. Roger’s frown deepened, but even he seemed unsure what to say to a version of Eira that refused to shrink.","The front door opened.","\"Sorry, I’m late.\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice sounded almost cheerful.","Eira turned.","He was not alone.","A woman stood beside him in a cream coat that cost more than Eira’s monthly salary on paper. Brown curls framed a delicate face. Her makeup was soft, her smile softer, and every inch of her seemed designed to make other women appear either plain or loud.","Alpha Sebastian held her coat sleeve lightly as he guided her inside.","\"I ran into Serena on the way back,\" he said. \"Serena Winthrop. A close friend from when I was young.\"","Close friend.","Serena’s overpoweringly strong perfume slid into the room and wrapped around Eira’s memory like a snake.","Alpha Sebastian turned to her with the calm smile he used at business dinners. \"Eira Crawford. My Luna.\"","Eira looked at Alpha Sebastian’s hand on Serena’s waist.","Alpha Sebastian did not notice it at first. Serena did. Her eyes flicked down, then up to Eira’s face, and her smile deepened by the smallest possible degree.","Some women needed knives. Serena Winthrop had dimples.","\"It’s so nice to finally meet you,\" Serena said, extending her hand. \"Sebastian talks about you all the time.\"","Eira glanced at the offered hand, then took it lightly. Serena’s fingers were soft and cool. Her grip tightened just enough to pretend warmth while testing strength.","\"How generous of him,\" Eira said. \"What exactly does he say?\""]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5 Unexpected Encounter","paragraphs":["Serena’s smile paused. \"Only good things, of course. He says you’re very helpful at home and that you manage Pack matters well. For an Omega to do so much, it’s really impressive.\"","There it was. The compliment with a collar around its neck.","\"It is impressive,\" Eira said. \"Managing a Pack, working full-time, handling his family’s problems, and welcoming old friends who arrive without warning—all on such a small allowance. I impress myself sometimes.\"","Isabella blinked. Margaret’s face tightened. Alpha Sebastian gave Eira a warning look, which she carefully ignored.","Serena withdrew her hand. \"You’re funny.\"","\"No,\" Eira said. \"Just accurate.\"","Dinner, when it finally arrived by delivery, was a miserable experience for everyone except Eira. That alone improved her appetite. The poached shrimp were bland, the broccoli looked depressed, and Margaret stared at the plastic containers as if Eira had personally dragged the Hale bloodline into the gutter.","Serena, of course, ate three bites and praised the food with saintly patience.","\"This is actually very healthy,\" she said. \"I admire women who can keep a household simple.\"","\"I admire women who can keep their hands off married men,\" Eira replied, reaching for her water.","The table went silent.","Alpha Sebastian’s fork stopped halfway to his mouth. \"Eira.\"","\"What?\" She looked at him. \"We’re admiring women. I wanted to join.\"","Serena’s eyes grew bright, but no tears fell. Too skilled for that. \"I’m sorry if my being here makes you uncomfortable. Alpha Sebastian and I have known each other since childhood. I used to belong here too. Sebastian is like family to me.\"","\"So why’d you leave back then? Was this Pack too poor for you?\"","Margaret slammed her glass down. \"Enough. Serena is a guest.\"","\"But she just said you’re family. Doesn’t that make me the guest in this house?\"","\"Shut your mouth, Eira.\" Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"Remember you are Luna.\"","\"I remember better than anyone,\" Eira said. \"For instance, before this Pack got rich, I never once heard the name Serena mentioned. You should try respecting that.\"","Alpha Roger watched her more carefully now. He was not kind, but he understood numbers and power better than Margaret did.","Problems were harder to throw away than tools.","Isabella ruined the tension by noticing Serena’s bag. \"Oh my god, is that the limited Virelle piece? I saw it in a magazine. It’s over a hundred thousand.\"","Serena glanced down with perfect modesty. \"A gift from a friend.\"","Her eyes went to Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyebrow moved by a fraction.","Eira saw it. She also saw the small logo, the same brand as the silk scarf Alpha Sebastian had offered her that morning. The main gift had gone to Serena. The apology scrap had been meant for the wife.","A comfort prize for the tool.","\"A gift from a friend?\" Eira said, looking at the bag, then at Alpha Sebastian. \"Your friends have excellent taste. Very similar to my husband’s.\"","Serena’s fingers tightened on the chain strap. Alpha Sebastian’s face remained controlled, but his scent sharpened. He knew she had hit close to something.","For the rest of dinner, Margaret tried to guide every topic back to Serena’s virtues. International education. Winthrop Pack connections. Her father’s influence. Her suitable bloodline. Her bright future. Each subject was placed on the table like an offering to Alpha Sebastian, and each one reminded everyone that Eira had arrived in Hale Pack with no family name worth announcing.","Eira let them talk.","Her bag sat by her chair. Inside it, the agreement waited beneath routine Pack finance documents.","Timing mattered. Alpha Sebastian had to be relaxed enough to sign, but irritated enough not to read.","Serena’s presence helped. Men like Alpha Sebastian became careless when they wanted to prove control in front of women.","After dessert, Serena placed a hand against her temple. \"Oh dear, it’s getting late. I should go. I’m still tired from my flight. I’m afraid I might fall asleep while driving.\"","Isabella leaned forward at once. \"Sebastian, you should drive her home. It’s not safe for Serena to go alone.\"","Margaret nodded. \"Of course. A gentleman should.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked from Serena to Eira. He performed hesitation well. \"Why don’t you stay at our place for now? You shouldn’t drive tired.\"","Serena turned her eyes toward Eira. \"Are you sure? Won’t Eira mind?\"","Eira laughed once. Cold and short. \"Why would I mind? If he enjoys collecting lost dogs and bringing them inside, I’m not the animal control department.\"","Serena’s face went pale with theatrical hurt.","\"That’s enough,\" Alpha Sebastian said. His voice dropped into Alpha command. \"Apologize.\"","Eira stood and picked up her bag. \"No.\"","His eyes flashed. \"Eira.\"","She looked at him across the table, at the husband who had called her useful, the Alpha who thought his title could still bend her spine. \"You can host whoever you want. You can buy whatever gifts you want. You can even ask everyone here to pretend they don’t smell another woman on you. But don’t ask me to decorate the lie.\"","The silence after that was sharp enough to cut skin.","Before Alpha Sebastian could answer, Eira walked out.","She drove back to Sterling Hotel with both hands on the wheel. It was 9:40 p.m. when she reached the underground garage. Only then did her stomach growl so loudly she almost laughed. She had eaten barely anything at dinner. Anger, it turned out, was not a balanced meal.","The hotel restaurant was closing when she reached the lobby level. Staff were clearing the last tables, and the lights had dimmed to a warm amber.","\"Sorry, miss,\" a waiter said. \"The kitchen closed ten minutes ago.\"","\"Bread is enough,\" Eira said. \"Or anything cold.\"","The waiter hesitated.","A voice came from the far end of the restaurant. \"Open the kitchen for her.\"","Eira turned.","The man from the elevator sat alone at a table near the windows. His dark shirt sleeves were rolled up, and a stack of papers lay beside a half-empty cup of coffee.","The waiter straightened so fast Eira heard his spine reconsider its life choices. \"Yes, Boss.\"","He didn’t get up. Didn’t even look particularly interested in his own generosity.","He just reached over, turned one of the papers face-down without breaking eye contact with her, and tapped two fingers against the empty chair across from him.","Then he tilted his head toward it, slow and deliberate, like he already knew she’d say yes and was just being polite about the wait.","\"Come sit,\" he said. \"Unless you want to eat standing.\""]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6 Perfect Setup","paragraphs":["\"How do you know I’ll come over?\"","\"I don’t. But the kitchen only cooks for people who are sitting.\"","\"Whose rule?\"","\"Mine.\"","Eira stared at him for two seconds, then walked over and sat across from him. Not because of him. Because she was hungry. That was all.","Mostly.","\"Are you going to thank me?\" he asked.","\"For what? Yesterday’s slippers or today’s bread?\"","\"Either is acceptable.\"","\"Depends on whether the bread is good. I already thanked you for the slippers. One item at a time.\"","His mouth moved slightly, as if he had almost smiled and decided it was bad for his brand. \"You keep careful accounts.\"","\"It’s a habit. For four years, I managed money for a whole family. Every favor given, every debt owed, every unpaid bill. I remember all of it.\"","\"Sounds like work.\"","\"It is.\" Eira looked toward the kitchen lights. \"What’s harder is when the owner of the money thinks the work does itself.\"","The words came out before she could stop them. She looked back at him. \"Sorry. You opened a kitchen, not a complaint office.\"","\"I didn’t offer dinner,\" he said. \"The kitchen is open. You pay.\"","Eira paused.","Then she laughed.","It startled her. The sound was small, rough, and real. The first real laugh she had made in what felt like years.","\"Fine,\" she said. \"Then I owe you nothing.\"","His gaze rested on her for a moment. \"Good.\"","Soup and bread arrived, along with butter and a small plate of sliced fruit she had not ordered. Eira ate without pretending elegance. Alpha Killian read his papers and drank cold coffee. The quiet between them did not demand performance. That made it rare.","When the waiter brought the bill, Alpha Killian reached for it.","Eira put her card down first. \"No.\"","His brows lifted.","\"You said I pay,\" she reminded him. \"Don’t ruin a good rule.\"","After a pause, he leaned back. \"Fair.\"","The waiter took her card. For some reason, paying for soup felt better than receiving diamonds from Alpha Sebastian ever had.","When she stood, Alpha Killian did not stand too quickly or try to walk her upstairs. He only said, \"Good night, Miss Crawford.\"","\"Good night, Mr. Sterling.\"","His eyes sharpened slightly.","She gave him a tired smile. \"Boss, remember?\"","--","The next morning, Eira went back to the apartment.","She opened the door. What she saw made her stop cold.","Serena lay stretched across the sofa. She wore thin, see-through clothes. So she had actually stayed.","In the kitchen stood Alpha Sebastian. He had never cooked a day in his life. He was making breakfast for her.","The sight was almost funny.","Alpha Sebastian hated the smell of cooking. He hated it so much that he had vetoed an open kitchen when they renovated, because he didn’t want the smell touching his suits.","For four years, Eira had cooked behind a closed kitchen door, so that no trace of it would ever reach him.","Apparently, the rule only applied to her.","\"See that?\" Serena tilted her chin toward the kitchen. She was proud. \"Do you get it now, Eira? This is the real him. You were just—\"","She smiled. It was too sweet. \"—someone he used until I came back.\"","She paused. She let her words sink in.","\"A stand-in. Nothing more.\"","\"So what?\" Eira said. \"Are you asking him to end our bond?\"","Serena’s face showed a quick flash of confusion.","Then she quickly put on her proud face again. She straightened her back. \"He will. It’s just a matter of time.\"","\"Good,\" Eira said. \"Go ahead.\"","She meant it. She really wanted him to sign those papers.","Serena clearly didn’t expect Eira’s answer. She froze. She couldn’t get her thoughts in order.","Just then, Alpha Sebastian came out of the kitchen.","He carried a hot cup of mint tea. He saw Eira’s face. He stopped for a moment.","\"Serena’s not feeling well.\" He explained before Eira could ask. \"I’m making her something warm for her stomach.\"","His fingers were red from the heat. It was likely the first time he had carried something hot without protecting his hands.","He deserved it. Let it burn.","Then he handed the cup straight to Eira. \"I’ll get a heating pad. Give this to her.\"","The ceramic cup was so hot, Eira could barely hold it.","Serena lay on the sofa. Her lips curved up. Like she was taking a gift. \"Thanks so much, Eira.\"","Eira held out the cup. Serena reached for it.","The cup tilted a little. A few drops of tea splashed on Serena’s hand.","That was all. Not even enough to make a small bubble.","But Serena gasped. Like she had been hit with boiling oil. She quickly pulled her hand back. Her eyes filled with tears.","Her reaction was very fast. Faster than real pain would make it.","\"Ah...\"","Alpha Sebastian ran over at once. He grabbed Serena’s wrist to check it. Then he turned to Eira and shouted, \"What happened?\"","\"She pulled her hand back,\" Eira said. Her voice was flat.","He didn’t believe her.","He looked down at Serena’s hand. The few drops of tea were still there. They hadn’t even dried.","Then he looked up at Eira. His eyes turned cold.","\"You did that on purpose.\"","Just those five words.","No questions. No proof.","He just decided it was Eira’s fault.","Eira calmly put the teacup back on the table. It made a soft sound as it touched the wood.","Behind him, Serena spoke softly. \"Sebastian, just forget it... It doesn’t hurt that much...\"","Her voice shook in just the right way.","That sentence was like a key. It opened the last little bit of doubt Alpha Sebastian had.","\"Eira.\" His voice was low. Like a verdict. \"Apologize.\"","She didn’t move.","\"I said, apologize.\"","The air was very still for two seconds.","Eira looked at him. Suddenly, the word \"apologize\" coming from his mouth seemed more silly than the hot tea.","\"Fine,\" she said. \"I’ll say sorry.\"","His face relaxed a little. Then Eira bent down. She picked up the cup she had just put down. It was still more than half full.","\"Eira?\"","She stood up. She poured all the tea over Serena’s face."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7 Hidden in Plain Sight","paragraphs":["The liquid ran down Serena’s hair. It made her clothes wet. It went down her neck and into her dress.","Serena screamed. She jumped up. She looked like a wet, angry cat.","Alpha Sebastian stood still. He looked shocked.","\"That cup, I actually threw,\" Eira said. \"So when you say I did it, at least you’ll be right.\"","Alpha Sebastian suddenly moved. His face darkened completely. \"Are you crazy?!\"","\"I’m not crazy,\" Eira said. She put the empty cup back on the table. \"I just don’t like being blamed for things I didn’t do. If you want to yell at me, yell about what I really did. Don’t punish me for things I never touched.\"","\"You—\" He started to say more.","\"You will take care of Serena until she gets better.\"","Eira stopped and turned to look at him.","\"You hurt her, so you’re responsible.\" He said it.","His jaw was tight. \"And you should feel good about it. Serena’s talent is irreplaceable for her work. Taking care of her yourself is a chance most people would beg for.\"","\"You want me to stop working and be her full-time nurse?\" Eira paused. Like the idea just came to her. \"If you really think I should be ready to help her all the time, I can leave Sterling Group for good. I won’t go back.\"","That made him stop. The anger on his face went away. Something else took its place. He looked careful. \"You’re serious.\"","\"Completely serious.\" Eira took her coat off the hook. \"I’ll quit all my jobs. I’ll stay home and be your Luna. But only if you transfer this house into my name.\"","He was quiet for a few seconds. His eyes narrowed, as if searching for the trap.","But what trap could there be? A wolfless Omega with no family and no backing, asking for the one apartment she lived in. It was exactly what an orphan would want. Security. A roof that couldn’t be taken away.","If anything, it proved she was finally thinking like a proper Luna. Staying home. Needing him.","\"Deal.\"","Alpha Sebastian didn’t waste time.","At four o’clock that afternoon, they met in his office.","Eira pushed the folder across the desk.","The paper for the house transfer sat on top. Clean. Easy to read. Impossible to miss.","Right behind it, in the same font and format, was the document ending their mate bond.","It was just there. Waiting for someone to read it.","Sebastian reached for his pen, then paused. For the first time, some instinct made him pick up the folder itself instead of just the signature line. He started flipping through the pages, actually reading them.","Eira’s pulse spiked. She kept her face still, but her fingers curled slightly at her side.","Sebastian glanced up and caught it. The flicker in her eyes, gone almost as fast as it appeared. It was enough to make him slow down even more. He turned back to the first page, this time scanning every line instead of skimming.","His finger stopped near the middle of the stack, right where the mate dissolution clause began.","His phone rang.","Serena.","He looked at the screen, then back at the folder, caught in the middle.","\"I gotta take this.\" He grabbed his jacket.","Eira’s stomach dropped. If he walked out with the folder still open, he’d come back and actually find it.","She grabbed his sleeve.","\"You’re already here. Just sign and go. I’ll handle the rest.\"","Her tone stayed flat, bored, like she couldn’t care less.","Sebastian glanced at her hand, then at his buzzing phone.","He sat back down.","He signed the house transfer, then flipped straight to the signature lines on the divorce papers without reading another word, phone still buzzing in his other hand.","Page after page, no hesitation, straight to the last line.","\"That’s it?\"","\"That’s it.\" Eira snapped the folder shut before he could change his mind.","Sebastian was already answering the call on his way out, his voice softening the second he heard Serena.","No goodbye. Eira didn’t look back either.","Thirty days. That’s what the paper said.","In thirty days, Alpha Sebastian Hale and Eira Crawford would be strangers.","No ties left at all.","--","Eira had just stepped out of Hale Tower when Alpha Sebastian’s private car pulled up.","Four years of marriage, and this was the first time he’d actually sent a car for her. Usually, he’d just say, \"Figure it out yourself.\"","Thirty minutes later, the Bentley parked outside Sterling Tower.","\"We’re here, Luna Eira.\" The Hale family driver opened the door for her.","\"Thanks. You can go back now.\" She put her resignation letter under her arm.","\"Alpha Sebastian will want to know what happened.\"","\"He’ll find out soon enough.\"","She walked to the door. She used her face to open it.","She had never really worked here. This job was just a secret place for her. A place to hide when she needed to.","Now, to end it, she only needed to go to one person: Vanessa Cole in HR.","Before Eira even got to the front desk, Vanessa saw her. Vanessa had a cup of coffee. Her face looked surprised. \"Eira! I didn’t think I’d see you here.\"","\"Do you have a minute?\"","\"Of course. Come on in.\" Vanessa waved to her office. She was very friendly. That’s how she was with people connected to important bosses.","Halfway there, Eira felt a strange feeling on her neck. Someone was watching her.","She turned. She only saw a shoulder. A dark jacket. It turned a corner to the boss’s elevator.","It looked familiar. But she couldn’t remember why.","\"Are you okay?\" Vanessa asked.","\"Someone was watching us just now.\"","Vanessa looked where Eira pointed. She saw nothing. She laughed a little. \"You’re probably just imagining things.\"","\"That elevator.\" Eira pointed to it.","Vanessa’s smile froze. \"Which elevator?\"","\"That one.\"","\"You must have seen wrong.\" Vanessa swallowed. \"That’s our boss’s private elevator. He never even looks at HR. He wouldn’t be standing around here.\"","Vanessa’s office door said \"Vice President of Human Resources.\" She got a promotion since Eira was last here.","\"Congrats on the new job.\"","\"Thanks.\" Vanessa still looked worried about the elevator comment.","Eira didn’t waste time. \"I’m here to quit.\"","\"Oh. Okay. How fast do you need it done?\"","\"The usual time is fine.\"","\"The usual time is thirty days. But for your job, we can probably finish it in two or three days.\" Vanessa was already looking at forms on her computer.","Neither of them thought this would soon become a very big deal to someone important.","Five minutes after Eira left, someone knocked on Vanessa’s door.","\"Come in.\" She stood up even before she finished speaking. \"Miles.\"","\"Alpha Killian wants to see you.\"","[Oh no. Here comes my big test.] Vanessa thought to herself. [This was bad timing.]","The Sterling Group had been cleaning house for months, ever since that scandal where someone important embezzled over eight million. That’s how Vanessa got her promotion to VP of HR just six weeks ago.","She tried to think. Who could be causing trouble? She quickly scanned the new hires.","Only one name made her nervous: Eira Crawford.","But Eira had come through the Sterling family. Approved from the top. A favor for a favor. Low-level position, a salary that only existed on paper.","What could possibly be wrong with that?","...Right?","\"Give me a second,\" she said to Eira’s empty chair. Her voice was steady.","But as soon as she went outside, her calm look broke. \"Miles, is something wrong?\"","He fixed his glasses. He smiled. It was a smile that didn’t help her at all. \"You’ll see when you get there.\""]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8 The Compliance Hold","paragraphs":["Eira had barely stepped out of Hale Tower when Alpha Sebastian’s private car slid up to the curb.","Four years of marriage. This was the first time he’d ever sent a car for her.","The Bentley stopped outside Sterling Tower.","\"We’re here, Luna Eira.\" The driver came around and opened her door.","\"Thank you. You can head back now.\" She tucked the resignation letter under her arm.","\"Alpha Sebastian asked to be told where you went.\"","\"He’ll find out soon enough.\"","She walked to the entrance and let the scanner read her face.","Vanessa Cole. HR.","Vanessa spotted her before she reached the desk, coffee frozen halfway to her mouth. Surprise flashed across her face, then smoothed into the bright, syrupy warmth she saved for anyone tied to someone important. \"Eira! I didn’t expect to see you here today.\"","\"Do you have a minute?\"","\"Of course. Come in.\"","Halfway across the lobby, the back of Eira’s neck prickled.","Someone was watching her.","She turned.","She caught only the edge of it — a shoulder, a dark jacket, the clean line of an expensive sleeve rounding the corner toward the executive elevator. Gone in a second.","But something in the set of those shoulders snagged on a memory she couldn’t quite reach. Like a name on the tip of her tongue that refused to arrive.","\"Everything okay?\" Vanessa asked.","\"Someone was watching us just now.\"","Vanessa followed her gaze to the empty corridor and laughed lightly. \"You’re imagining things. Long day?\"","\"That elevator.\" Eira nodded at it. \"Someone stepped off and went that way.\"","Vanessa’s smile froze at the corners. \"...Which elevator?\"","\"That one.\"","\"You must’ve seen wrong.\" She swallowed. The sound was audible. \"That’s the boss’s private elevator. He never comes down to HR. He wouldn’t just be standing around a lobby.\"","Eira let it go.","It wasn’t her problem anymore. In ten minutes, nothing in this building would be.","The plaque on Vanessa’s door read Vice President of Human Resources. New, since the last time.","\"Congratulations on the promotion.\"","\"Thank you.\" But Vanessa kept glancing back at that corridor, like she expected it to open its mouth and swallow her whole.","Eira sat, laid the letter on the desk, and didn’t waste words. \"I’m here to resign.\"","\"Oh. Right.\" Vanessa pulled up the forms on autopilot. \"How fast do you need it processed?\"","\"Standard timing is fine.\"","\"Standard is thirty days. Though for your position, honestly, we can close it in two or three. There’s not much to unwind.\"","Eira signed where she was told, set down the pen, and felt something in her chest go quiet.","That was it. The last thread. Cut.","--","Five minutes after Eira left, a knock landed on Vanessa’s door.","\"Come in—\" She was already on her feet before the word finished. \"Miles.\"","\"Alpha Killian wants to see you.\"","Vanessa’s stomach dropped straight through the floor.","Killian had summoned her exactly once since her promotion. That meeting had ended with two directors walked out of the building by security.","Sterling Group had been bleeding out its rot for months — ever since the embezzlement scandal. The one where a name too senior to touch had quietly walked off with north of eight million before the Council pried it loose.","The purge that followed was how a mid-level HR manager had become a Vice President in six weeks.","Her mind raced through every new hire. Every flag. Every file that could’ve caught the wrong eye.","Only one name made her palms go cold.","Eira Crawford.","But no. Eira was clean. She’d come in through the Sterling family itself, approved from somewhere above Vanessa’s clearance. A favor for a favor. A nothing role. A salary that lived mostly on paper.","There was nothing there to find.","...Right?","--","Alpha Killian’s monitor was still open to the same email. He’d read it twice. Hated it both times.","FROM: Council Registrar’s Office","RE: Formal Notice — Luna Candidacy Review, Q3","Nine names. Nine daughters from nine allied Packs. Nine headshots posed and polished like a dating profile no one had asked to see.","He had zero interest in any of them.","The door opened, cutting the thought off cold.","Vanessa stepped in. He didn’t look up.","\"The woman you just met with. Who is she?\"","\"Uh — Eira Crawford.\"","Crawford.","His pen stopped moving.","The same surname he’d been chasing for three days. Same height. Same careful way of holding herself.","He opened her file himself.","It loaded fast. Because there was almost nothing to load.","One photo. She looked younger. Her eyes were sharper, less worn down.","So the barefoot ghost from three nights ago in Room 1806 had a first name now.","Eira.","\"Explain.\"","Sweat surfaced along Vanessa’s hairline. \"Your aunt — Marnie — brought her in, Alpha Killian. The file’s low-access. Office support, nothing sensitive. She never touched anything confidential.\"","\"My aunt.\"","Marnie hadn’t touched company business in a decade. She wouldn’t forward a résumé.","\"Check her. Dig deeper. Find everything.\"","\"Right away.\" Miles slipped out.","\"She actually came in today to quit,\" Vanessa added. She hoped that would help.","It did not help. If anything, it made the whole thing worse.","Something in Alpha Killian’s chest tightened before his brain caught up with it — the same feeling as watching a door start to close from across the room, too far away to reach it in time.","A check like this usually took thirty minutes. This one took ten.","Ten minutes meant there was almost nothing to find.","Miles came back with one thin paper. Sweat was near his temple. \"This is everything, Alpha Killian.\"","An orphan. An Omega. A brilliant degree — and no record of the years that should have surrounded it. No hometown. No family. After graduation, a flat, echoing blank: no jobs, no leases, no accounts any system would admit to.","\"A file this clean is not by chance,\" Miles said. \"Someone made it look this way.\"","In other words, she was not just \"nobody.\"","Whoever she was, someone had worked very hard to make sure no one could find out.","Alpha Killian’s face grew dark. This was more than just being curious now. A woman whose past was erased on purpose.","She was secretly put into his company."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9 The Performance","paragraphs":["Eira arrived home at six in the evening.","Alpha Sebastian was sprawled on the couch, watching her with that familiar look—the one that said she’d already done something wrong before she’d even opened her mouth.","\"You’re late.\"","\"And you’re early.\" She raised an eyebrow. \"Thought you’d be playing chauffeur all night.\"","His jaw tightened. He didn’t take the bait. Instead, he jumped straight to what was really bothering him. \"An administrative position. And it takes a month to process a resignation?\"","\"Company policy.\"","She turned to leave. His hand shot out and caught her wrist.","\"I’m hungry.\"","Four years. And this was the first time she heard it clearly—this was never a request. It was a command.","\"Go make dinner. I want that braised beef my mother taught you.\"","\"There’s nothing fresh in the house.\"","\"Then go buy some.\"","\"At this hour? Everything’s closed.\"","He frowned at her like she were deliberately stalling.","She kept her tone casual. \"You should probably check on Serena’s hand. Make sure she didn’t bruise anything.\"","His grip loosened instantly. The speed at which he pulled out his phone was almost funny.","\"I’m still at Silix Institute,\" came Serena’s voice through the speaker, breathy and deliberately sweet.","Eira froze.","Silix Institute. Where she worked.","But she’d never seen Serena in that building. Never heard anyone mention \"Serena Winthrop\" by name.","Except—","A conversation surfaced in her mind.","Last week her assistant had come in with coffee, venting about some director’s granddaughter angling for a spot at the institute.","A resume built for magazine covers. International scholarships. Co-authored papers. A grandfather who made calls to open doors.","\"Sharp instincts, though,\" her assistant had said, rolling her eyes. \"Wonder what she’s after this time.\"","Eira had shrugged it off and forgotten about it.","Now, listening to that same fake breathless voice on the phone, it all clicked.","\"What do you want to eat? I’ll have Eira make it for you.\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice dripped with false tenderness. That alone snapped her back to the moment.","\"Are you sure that’s okay?\"","\"Of course it’s okay. Your hand got hurt because of her. It’s the least she can do.\"","Serena ordered braised beef short ribs—with herb butter, fresh thyme, and shallots. All fresh ingredients. At this hour, impossible to find.","Eira knew exactly what this was. A dish deliberately chosen because it couldn’t be made on short notice.","\"I’m not hungry,\" Eira said. \"You two enjoy.\"","\"I mean you cook it. She’ll eat it when she gets here.\"","\"Am I the hired help now, Sebastian?\"","\"Her hand got hurt because of you. You’re responsible for taking care of her until it heals.\"","\"I didn’t hurt her.\"","He wasn’t listening. In this house, facts had never mattered.","\"Braised short ribs. Tonight.\"","One more month. Just get through it.","\"Fine.\" She swallowed the anger rising in her throat. \"You go pick her up. I’ll cook.\"","The door closed behind him.","Then Eira pulled out her phone, opened a delivery app, and ordered braised beef short ribs with roasted vegetables.","The food arrived before they did. She transferred the ribs into a still-warm cast-iron pot and scattered the last of the parsley from the fridge over the vegetables.","It smelled right. Looked right. Like she’d made it herself.","Who would look closely enough to tell the difference?","--","On her way back from throwing out the delivery containers, Eira heard laughter from the corner of the street.","Serena had one hand over her mouth, doubled over. Alpha Sebastian reflexively reached out to steady her, saw Eira, and froze. His hand hung in midair before he pulled it back.","\"Eira? What are you doing out here?\"","\"Taking out the trash.\"","She headed for the door, tuning out whatever story they were reminiscing about—some trip from their youth, probably.","Just before she closed the door, Serena’s voice drifted over again.","\"Oh, Sebastian,\" she said lightly, like it was an afterthought, \"Did I tell you? I’m joining a federal-level project next week.\"","\"What project?\"","\"Chip development. The details aren’t public yet.\" She laughed, pride unmistakable in her tone. \"I heard it’s groundbreaking. Even the federal government’s watching it closely.\"","Eira’s footsteps stopped.","A federal chip project big enough to have Washington watching. There weren’t many of those. And the one that mattered was hers.","Serena. It had to be Serena.","There was only one way Serena could already know the results were about to go public. Someone with real access had told her. Her grandfather.","As for why Serena had never seen her at Silix, the answer was simple. The core team’s roster was locked down. No outsider got the list. Whatever Serena knew, she’d gotten secondhand, filtered through whatever her grandfather chose to repeat.","She didn’t even know the woman she’d been mocking all evening was the one who ran it.","--","The five minutes before dinner were quiet.","Serena poked at the meat on her plate with her fork, then asked, seemingly casual, who’d taught Eira to make this dish.","\"Google.\"","\"Wow.\" Serena’s smile was loaded. \"First time making it, and it turned out pretty good.\"","Eira didn’t bite.","Serena kept going, riding the high of a win she hadn’t even landed yet.","\"My grandfather’s been on the phone all week,\" she said, practically glowing. \"Once this hits the news, my name’s going to be everywhere.\"","\"Sounds like you’ve got it all figured out,\" Eira said.","\"Obviously.\" Serena raised an eyebrow, fishing for a compliment.","\"So. You earn this? Or your grandfather did?\"","Serena blinked. Then laughed, sharp and fake. \"Excuse me? You think I don’t deserve it?\"","\"Didn’t say that.\" Eira shrugged. \"Just wondering if whoever actually did the work knows you’re about to take a bow for it.\"","Serena’s smile cracked.","\"Wow, rude much?\" She turned to Alpha Sebastian, voice going all soft and hurt. \"You hear that?\"","Alpha Sebastian shot Eira a look. \"Ease up. She earned this. Not everyone gets that kind of break.\"","\"I’m being nice.\" Eira raised her glass. \"I just didn’t clap for her.\"","Dead silence.","Serena had nothing. Because Eira hadn’t said a thing that was technically wrong. She just wasn’t playing along, and everyone at the table knew it.","Alpha Sebastian glanced at Eira, opened his mouth, thought better of it, and turned back to patch things up with Serena.","Eira put her fork down. \"Full.\"","\"You didn’t even finish half of it.\"","\"Full.\"","He shook his head, gave up. \"Suit yourself.\"","--","Eira was mid-change when the door banged open.","\"That wasn’t your cooking.\" Flat. No heat, just fact. \"Four years of your food. I know the taste. You never load up on sugar like that.\"","\"Wow.\" She turned around, one shoulder lifting in a shrug. \"Didn’t know you had taste buds. Go be a food critic or something.\"","He didn’t bite. \"What’s your deal lately? You’re dodging me.\"","\"Doing my job.\"","\"As my Luna—\"","\"As your Luna, I run this house. Done. What you want? Different story.\"","He closed the gap. \"We haven’t shared a bed in days.\"","\"And?\"","\"Just sleep tonight. That’s all.\"","She stayed quiet. He read that as a yes.","His mouth pressed to her forehead. She didn’t lean in. Didn’t pull back either. Just stood there like furniture.","Then a crash from the hallway. \"Ow—Sebastian?\"","He bailed and yanked the door open.","Serena was on the floor, suitcase flipped on its side. \"Wheel got stuck. Whole thing landed on my foot.\"","He was already scooping her up, one arm under her knees, the other catching her back.","She shot Eira a smirk over his shoulder, then instantly switched to wounded puppy. \"Lost a slipper.\"","\"Grab it later.\"","Footsteps faded down the hall.","Eira shut the door and sagged against it, breathing out hard.","Dodged that one. Serena would drag out the drama for a solid half hour. Perfect window for a shower, a locked door, and playing dead.","But this wasn’t going to work forever.","Tonight it was a suitcase. Tomorrow? She wasn’t betting the house on some she-wolf tripping over her own baggage every single time.","She needed something bulletproof. A reason he couldn’t talk his way out of."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10 The Sterling Archives","paragraphs":["To find out who Eira Crawford was, Killian would have to go home first.","And going home was never simple.","Sterling Manor didn’t sit on the mountain. It owned the mountain—three hundred years of pine forest, a private road, and stone walls that had never once changed hands. People had tried. Their names were on tombstones now.","Three black SUVs cleared the checkpoints without slowing and rolled to a stop before the main house.","Killian stepped out. Night wind caught his dark hair; he shoved it back, silver-gray eyes cold under the estate lights.","He’d barely crossed the courtyard when a metallic crash rang out from the workshop.","\"Killian! If you still claim me as your sister, get in here and pretend you understand processors!\"","He didn’t break stride. \"Love you. Not that much.\"","\"Liar.\" Lila stuck her head out, screwdriver jammed in her hair, solder ash on one cheek. \"I’m your only sister.\"","\"That’s not a selling point. That’s biology.\"","She rolled her eyes and dragged out a half-finished prototype, wires spilling from its open chest like torn veins.","\"My son’s dying,\" she announced.","\"Your board’s fried.\" He barely glanced at it. \"Chip ceiling.\"","Lila’s face fell. \"I hate it when you’re right.\"","\"You hate it because I’m always right.\"","She flipped him off but followed anyway. \"Tell me Sterling Group has better chips.\"","\"We don’t.\"","\"Tell me you bought out some lab with a breakthrough.\"","\"Also no.\"","\"Then why do you look like you already found the answer?\"","Killian stopped. He didn’t answer that.","\"Where’s Marnie?\"","Lila blinked, then narrowed her eyes and scanned him head to toe. \"You didn’t come home to see Mom and Dad. You didn’t come back for dinner either.\" A beat. \"You drove two hours for Aunt Marnie.\"","He just looked at her.","\"Fine.\" She jerked her chin up, annoyed. \"She hijacked my lab cart two hours ago—said she needed to haul some old foundation archives. I want it back. That thing’s irreplaceable.\"","They stopped at the end of the east wing. The old library.","Behind the heavy oak door sat three hundred years of Pack records—alliances, debts, marriage contracts, territorial disputes, blood feuds.","Lila studied his face. \"You’ve got that look. Like you just found a loaded gun and you’re deciding who gets the first bullet.\"","\"Dramatic.\"","\"But accurate.\"","He pushed the door open.","The room smelled of old leather, cold stone, and dying embers. Territorial maps hung on one wall; locked cabinets of foundation records and council archives lined the other.","Marnie Sterling stood at the long table—tailored forest-green silk, silver hair pinned up, pearl earrings catching the light. Not some idle relative living off the estate.","She ran the Sterling Foundation. Grants, charitable placements, political connections, social favors—and the quiet things that never touched paper. Most of it went through her hands.","She heard the door and looked up. \"If this is about the foundation audit, I already told finance to stop whining.\"","\"It’s not.\" He crossed the room without raising his voice. \"It’s about Eira Crawford.\"","The second the name dropped, something flickered across Marnie’s face. Just a flicker. But Killian saw it.","Even Lila, mid-reach for a file on the table, went still. She didn’t know Eira Crawford. But she knew anyone who could drive her brother two hours home in the dark to corner their aunt wasn’t a random name on a list.","The temperature in the library seemed to drop a few degrees.","\"Vanessa said you were the one who placed her at Sterling Group.\" He set it out flat. \"Miles ran her file. No hiring process. No interview. No department referral. No payroll trail. The only thing he could track was a paper authorization out of your office.\"","Marnie wasn’t Sterling Group’s HR director. She never touched day-to-day hiring. A regular employee should never have crossed her desk—and definitely shouldn’t have left nothing but a paper trail behind.","\"So why,\" Killian said, voice dropping, \"would a woman with no legitimate hiring record end up in Sterling Group’s most invisible admin seat—through your hand?\"","Marnie set the folder down slowly.","\"Beatrice Thorne came to me.\"","Lila’s head snapped up. \"Thorne? As in Alaric Thorne?\"","Marnie glanced at her. \"Yes.\"","\"The Sovereign Processor Initiative Alaric Thorne?\"","\"Yes.\"","The library went silent.","The Sovereign Processor Initiative. A classified federal project built to break the country’s dependency on foreign chip architecture. When its lead researcher, Alaric Thorne, died a few years back, the outside world assumed it had been shelved.","Lately the whispers had turned. Research circles, investment networks—the project wasn’t dead. It was rumored to be nearing federal procurement evaluation.","And now Eira Crawford’s name sat tied to the Thornes.","\"Beatrice had just lost her husband,\" Marnie went on. \"She was watching Alaric’s life’s work fall apart from the inside. When she came to me, she looked like she hadn’t slept in a month. She said she had a student who just needed a quiet job to get by.\" She met Killian’s eyes. \"I’d known Beatrice thirty years. That was the first time she ever asked me for anything. So I didn’t ask questions. I placed the girl and let it be.\"","\"You didn’t wonder why Beatrice Thorne would bury one of her students in my admin pool?\"","\"I assumed she had her reasons. Grieving women usually do.\" Marnie’s fingers tightened on the folder’s edge. Something shifted in her face—real worry, not guilt. \"Did the girl do something wrong?\"","\"No. She resigned.\"","Killian let it drop. Not because he was satisfied—because Marnie had told him everything she knew. Whatever was left to find wasn’t in this room.","That night, Sterling Manor went quiet. Killian didn’t.","He turned over. Sleep wasn’t coming. A widow’s grieving favor. An erased history. A dead federal chip project suddenly breathing again. And a Stanford engineer buried in a job that did nothing, married to a man who’d let her vanish out of it in thirty days. None of the pieces touched—and that was exactly what wouldn’t let him sleep.","1:17 a.m. Miles picked up on the second ring. \"Alpha Killian?\"","\"Run a full background on Eira Crawford. And on Sebastian Hale.\"","A pause. \"Standard intel, or Pack-level?\"","\"Pack-level.\"","Miles sat straight up. That word changed everything.","\"Marriage registration. Financial agreements. Mate bond filing. Bite-mark records. Medical authorizations. Joint accounts. Omega welfare audits.\" Killian’s voice didn’t slow. \"First draft on my desk before morning.\"","Miles almost asked why. A midnight Pack-level check on a married Omega and her husband didn’t sound like Killian at all. He swallowed it. \"Understood, Alpha Killian.\"","The call ended. Killian dialed again.","Vanessa’s phone buzzed her half-awake. One look at the screen and she was fully awake. \"Alpha Killian?\"","His voice stayed flat.","\"Nine a.m. Send Eira Crawford to my office.\""]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11 The Name Beneath the Papers","paragraphs":["The next morning.","Eira woke early. Gray-blue dawn light filtered through the curtain edges. She lay still for two seconds, then sat up.","Her phone buzzed on the nightstand.","Vanessa: Eira, your resignation process isn’t complete yet. You’ll need to report to the office as usual until your exit review is finalized.","Perfect. She needed a reason to get out of the Hale house. This worked.","Eira: Okay.","She washed up, changed clothes, grabbed her bag. But when she opened the bedroom door, she stopped.","Serena Winthrop stood in the hallway, leaning against the wall. Wearing a robe that didn’t belong to her.","Eira’s robe. The one missing from her closet.","Serena yawned like a cat just waking up, thick golden waves tumbling over her shoulders, green eyes half-lidded with lazy triumph. Like she was the real mistress of this house.","\"Morning, Eira.\"","Eira didn’t answer. She crouched down to tie her shoe.","Serena didn’t rush. She leaned back against the wall, gaze sliding slowly over Eira’s frame, like she was appraising a piece of old furniture about to be tossed out.","\"Your job at Sterling Group,\" Serena said suddenly. \"How far along is your resignation?\"","\"Still processing.\"","\"Processing.\" Serena let out a soft laugh. \"You know my grandfather has ties to the Sterling family, right? Winthrop Pack and Sterling Pack have had business dealings for years. I’ve even met Alpha Killian in person.\"","She paused, her face softening into something almost generous.","\"If you want to stay, I could put in a word for you. Get you transferred to a better position. Maybe a salary bump. That way Sebastian wouldn’t think your work is so... disposable.\"","Eira looked at her. Two seconds. Then she smiled. Calm. Controlled.","\"Sure.\"","Serena’s eyes flickered.","Eira picked up her bag and walked past her. \"I’ll wait for your call.\"","The door opened. Then closed.","Serena’s smile faded slowly in the empty hallway. Something felt off. Eira had been too calm. Not like a wolfless Omega who’d just been humiliated. But so what. Soon enough, she’d be gone for good, and everything would go back to the way it should be.","--","Eira left Hale territory behind and headed for the block outside Sterling Tower.","She grabbed a taco from one of the trucks lined up for the morning rush. Extra everything. The hottest salsa on the menu. First bite burned longer than she wanted to admit.","That was the wrong moment to look up.","Someone slammed into her at full speed. Like she was sprinting to catch a flight two gates over and losing.","Eira barely rocked back on her heels. The girl who hit her wasn’t so lucky. She stumbled, arms flailing. A stack of papers went flying, right there on the sidewalk in front of the Tower’s revolving doors.","Eira’s hand shot out on instinct. She caught the girl’s arm and steadied her before she hit the ground.","\"Whoa. You good?\"","Lila Sterling blinked up at her, a little dazed. No-frame glasses. A messy ponytail, the kind that said I have not slept and I do not care. Sharp cheekbones.","Lab rat energy, Lila thought immediately. Big time.","\"I’m — oh my God, I’m fine.\" Lila scrambled up, breathless, chasing runaway papers across the plaza before they hit the revolving doors.","Eira crouched to help and caught one page mid-air. One line of numbers stuck out. The kind of error that made her fingers itch before her brain finished deciding to care. She circled it, jotted the fix in the margin, and slid the page back into the stack.","\"You just saved my life,\" Lila said, clutching the papers to her chest like they were made of gold. \"Okay, not my life. My GPA. Same thing, basically.\"","\"No problem.\"","\"I am so late, I gotta run—\" Two steps toward the entrance, Lila spun back around. \"Wait! What’s your name? I owe you coffee! Like, real coffee, not the truck kind!\"","Her smile was so blinding, so completely unguarded, that Eira answered before she’d even decided to.","\"Eira.\"","\"Got it! Bye, Eira, you’re a lifesaver, literally, bye!\"","And she was gone. Sprinting through the revolving doors like the building was on fire. No idea her professor was about to look wrong.","Not far off, Vanessa watched the whole thing happen, coffee stopped halfway to her mouth.","Okay. So what even is this woman. Marnie pulls a favor to get her hired. Alpha Killian personally freezes her exit paperwork. Now Lila’s handing out coffee dates like candy. This entire family was losing it over one person.","\"Eira!\" Vanessa jogged over, all smiles. \"C’mon, follow me.\"","\"Hey, Vanessa. What’s up? This about my resignation?\"","They walked right past the HR elevators. The ones Eira actually knew.","\"This isn’t the way to your office,\" Eira said.","\"Nope. Executive floor.\" Vanessa said it flat, bored, like she’d rehearsed sounding bored in the mirror that morning. \"Alpha Killian’s EA is out on leave, and Legal decided exit paperwork this month gets signed off upstairs instead of by us. New policy. Didn’t write it. Don’t love it.\"","\"That’s a lot of hoops for a resignation.\"","\"Tell me about it. You’re the first one I’ve dragged up there. Lucky me.\" Vanessa rolled her eyes so hard it looked painful.","Her heels clicked down the hall like a countdown to something Eira wasn’t ready for. Not that anyone had bothered to warn her.","Straight up to the executive floor. Then they nearly ran smack into Miles, who looked like he’d pulled an all-nighter. Because he had. Deep-diving Eira’s entire life story.","Miles pushed his glasses up and hit her with a smile way too polished for a random Tuesday.","\"Miss Crawford.\"","Oh good. We’re doing formal now.","Since when? She glanced at the dark circles under his eyes. Whatever he’d been up all night doing, it ended with him knowing her last name before she’d said it.","Miles nodded at the double doors. \"Give it a minute. Alpha Killian’s still tied up.\"","--","Inside the office.","Lila slammed her research data onto her brother’s desk. It was basically a mic drop.","\"My professor says my numbers are off. They’re not.\" She’d been at this since midnight. Her eyes felt like sandpaper. \"Check them. Right now. Or I’m not walking at graduation.\"","Alpha Killian pinched the bridge of his nose. He already regretted letting her in.","He pulled the stack toward him. Flipped through two pages. Tapped a circled section without even really looking. \"You marked this yourself.\"","Lila squinted at the red ink. \"I didn’t circle this.\"","Alpha Killian’s voice went flat. \"Then Casper did.\"","\"Oh my God, wait, I remember now!\" Lila’s voice shot up an octave. \"The woman I ran into downstairs! It had to be her!\" She spun toward her brother, eyes huge. \"Is she in R&D? Total lab-coat vibes.\"","\"Who?\"","Lila kept going, ignoring him. \"Eira! Her name’s Eira. Is she in R&D or what?\"","The second that name left her mouth, Alpha Killian went stone still.","He grabbed the phone. Miles picked up on the first ring.","\"She here yet?\"","\"Yes, Alpha Killian.\"","\"Send her in.\"","Miles opened the door. \"Miss Crawford. Alpha Killian will see you now.\"","Eira stepped inside. The door clicked shut behind her. She glanced back once, then turned around.","That’s when she heard a voice she recognized.","\"Wait, coffee lady?! I mean, Eira! You’re actually here?\"","Eira’s head snapped up.","The girl from downstairs stood beside the desk, still clutching her papers like a lifeline.","A man sat in the chair behind the desk. Black dress shirt. Blood-red tie. The kind of face that made every she-wolf within a fifty-mile radius lose her train of thought mid-sentence and forget she even had one.","And he was staring straight at her.","Mr. Sterling. Recognition hit before her brain even caught up.","The guy from the elevator. The one who’d bought her soup and let her win the fight over the check.","Except he wasn’t just \"Mr. Sterling\" anymore. Alpha Killian, Miles had said. Same guy. Bigger office. Way worse timing.","Eira gave a small nod. \"Guilty as charged.\"","\"Knew it!\" Lila beamed. \"You just saved my whole thesis. Way more useful than my own brother.\" She spun back toward the desk, still grinning. Then she froze.","\"Wait.\" The smile dropped off her face. \"Eira?\" Her head whipped toward Alpha Killian. \"Isn’t this the woman you were ask—\"","\"Lila.\" One word. That was all it took.","Lila snapped her mouth shut.","Eira didn’t move. Something about that sentence hadn’t finished right.","Ask what?","The question sat there, unanswered, and refused to leave. It wasn’t the first time today someone had looked at her like they already knew something she hadn’t said out loud."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12 She Puts Up With Too Much","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian rose and took the marked page from Lila.","\"You made this correction?\"","\"Yes.\" Eira kept her voice even.","He studied the neat mark, then set the page down.","\"My executive assistant is on maternity leave. Recruiting hasn’t found a replacement.\"","\"I don’t have assistant experience.\"","\"You caught a graduate-level error in seconds. You can manage a calendar.\" His gaze stayed on hers. \"You’re already on payroll, and your resignation is still pending. Fill the position until your last day.\"","It sounded reasonable. Almost too reasonable.","Eira considered refusing, but that would only draw more attention. Accepting gave her time to decide whether Alpha Killian’s interest meant something or whether exhaustion had made her suspicious of everything.","\"Understood, Alpha Killian.\"","\"Start today. Miles will brief you.\"","Eira turned toward the door.","Lila caught up with her. \"Coffee. I still owe you.\"","\"Sure.\"","\"You coming?\" Lila asked her brother.","\"I’ve got somewhere to be.\" Alpha Killian was already grabbing his jacket. \"It’s on the way.\"","--","They landed at a window table.","The waiter set down three coffees. Alpha Killian slid one across the table without a word, sliding it in front of Eira before Lila could even reach for hers.","\"Thanks,\" Eira said. Then, quieter: \"Mr. Sterling.\"","Alpha Killian’s mouth curved. Slow. A little too relieved for a guy who’d spent the last hour acting like this was only about a vacant desk.","\"So you did remember.\"","Eira nodded. \"I did. And thanks. For everything, back then.\"","\"Wait, wait, wait.\" Lila sat up straight, looking between them like someone had switched channels mid-movie. \"What are you two even talking about? You’ve met before?\"","\"We ran into each other,\" Eira said simply. \"At a hotel.\"","\"Yep.\" Alpha Killian confirmed. Zero help whatsoever.","Lila’s jaw hit the floor. \"A hotel?! Oh my God. OH MY GOD.\" Her voice jumped an octave. She slapped both hands on the table. \"This is huge! Finally! Someone’s actually willing to put up with him! Someone might actually—\"","Alpha Killian’s hand shot out and clamped over her mouth.","Lila’s eyes went wide. She nodded like crazy. Universal sign language for okay, okay, I’ll shut up.","\"Sit. Still.\" Alpha Killian’s tone could freeze a glass of water mid-air. \"You’re twenty-two. Act like it.\"","He let go.","Lila slumped back in her chair with a huff. The second her brother’s attention drifted, she leaned across the table toward Eira.","\"Don’t let the scary-face thing fool you,\" she whispered, way too loud to actually count as whispering. \"He’s mean to your face and mean behind your back. Equal opportunity jerk.\"","Eira’s mouth twitched. Almost a smile.","\"That’s why nobody wants him,\" Lila went on, totally unbothered. \"The Pack Council’s basically been carpet-bombing his inbox with headshots of eligible she-wolves for months. Dude’s one bad Tuesday away from getting slapped into an arranged marriage.\"","Eira didn’t say anything. She just sipped her coffee, calm and composed, like the chaos around her had nothing to do with her at all.","Except it kind of did. Especially with Lila still going.","\"Okay, real question.\" Lila leaned across the table. \"You’re seriously not in R&D? Because you have major lab energy. I know the type. I spend every day with professors who smell like mothballs and burnt coffee.\"","She pointed at herself.","\"I’m twenty-two. I’m rich. I should be at brunch making bad decisions. Instead, I’m buried in equations because my robot child has expensive taste in processors.\"","Eira blinked.","\"And now you’re working upstairs? Killian already has two assistants, but neither of them handles his calendar. You’re filling in for his EA, which means you get the full nightmare package. Plus, weren’t you quitting anyway, so... ow!\"","Alpha Killian tapped the back of her hand.","\"You talk too much.\"","\"My bad. Should I communicate through intense eye contact and one-word answers like you?\"","She turned back to Eira.","\"Working for him is going to be brutal. Thoughts and prayers.\"","A small laugh slipped out of Eira.","Lila lit up. [She likes me. Nailed it.]","\"Anyway, thank you for catching me earlier. And for fixing my numbers. You saved my thesis and possibly my will to live.\"","She pulled out her phone.","\"We’re friends now. Give me your number. I promise I won’t blow up your phone. Maybe a few memes, the occasional crisis text, and emergency pizza invitations.\"","Eira hesitated, then took out her phone.","The screen flickered. Cracks spread across one corner.","Lila noticed but said nothing. She opened her contact card, and they tapped phones. Eira’s screen froze before the new contact finally appeared.","\"I haven’t been able to replace it,\" Eira said. \"Most of my paycheck goes toward household expenses.\"","Lila’s smile faded.","\"That’s generous, but it also sucks. Your family gets everything, and you get a phone held together by hope.\"","Eira had known her for less than an hour, yet Lila had noticed what the Hale family had ignored for four years.","Something warm stirred in her chest.","Then Alpha Killian spoke.","\"Alpha Sebastian makes millions, but his wife can’t replace a phone.\" His voice was quiet and cold. \"Hale Group must be doing worse than its press team claims.\"","Eira went still.","Vetted.","Miles knowing her full name before she introduced herself.","And now Alpha Killian knew who her husband was, how much he earned, and how their household money was spent.","The pieces finally clicked into place.","He had looked into her.","Not just her employee record. Her marriage.","The warmth inside her vanished. She felt exposed, as if he had opened a locked door without asking.","Alpha Killian saw the change in her face. The words had left him before caution caught up. He had meant to insult Alpha Sebastian, not remind Eira that he had been digging through her life.","Too late.","Eira put down her coffee and stood.","\"Lila, thank you for the coffee.\"","Then she turned to Alpha Killian, her expression calm again. Too calm.","\"Alpha Killian, what are my responsibilities?\"","\"Miles will brief you.\"","\"Understood.\"","She walked away without another word.","Alpha Killian watched her leave, jaw tight.","--","Thunk.","A hand stopped the elevator doors.","They reopened, and Alpha Killian stepped inside.","Eira moved aside. \"Alpha Killian.\"","\"Miss Crawford.\"","He glanced at her. The warmth from the café was gone.","\"I shouldn’t have mentioned your husband in front of Lila.\"","\"No, you shouldn’t have.\"","The elevator reached the executive floor. Alpha Killian let her exit first.","Miles was waiting outside.","He walked Eira through her temporary duties. She would manage Alpha Killian’s calendar, prepare meeting files, coordinate travel, and track partnerships.","Compared with running a federal research team, it was simple.","By noon, she had fixed two scheduling conflicts and caught an error in a partnership brief.","Miles reported back that afternoon.","\"Miss Crawford learns fast.\"","\"Good.\" Alpha Killian looked through the glass wall at her desk. Then he remembered the cracked phone. \"Sebastian Hale’s compensation.\"","Miles opened the file on his tablet. \"His disclosed base salary is close to five million a year. Not counting bonuses, dividends, or his shares in Hale Group.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression cooled. \"Yet his wife uses a broken phone and helps pay household expenses.\"","\"That’s what the records show.\"","\"Where does the rest go?\"","\"Corporate filings don’t show private spending. But last night’s Pack review found regular payments linked to Serena Winthrop. Research funding, travel, gifts.\" Miles paused. \"She also moved into the Hale residence.\"","\"You’ve been busy.\"","\"You ordered a Pack-level review.\"","Fair point.","Alpha Killian looked at Eira again. \"She puts up with too much.\"","Miles said nothing.","\"Send her in.\""]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13 Anything But Home","paragraphs":["Eira stepped into his office a minute later.","\"You wanted to see me?\"","Alpha Killian nodded toward a stack of reports on the side table.","\"Run the numbers, clean up the formatting, and flag anything that looks off. I need it by tomorrow afternoon.\"","Eira lifted the entire stack in one smooth motion.","Alpha Killian started to stand, but she already had the binders balanced against her hip.","\"Take two trips.\"","\"I’ve got it.\"","She walked out before he could argue.","Before lunch, Eira returned and placed her laptop on his desk.","\"Done.\"","Alpha Killian checked the time. \"Already?\"","\"Already.\"","He opened the file.","She had used the source data to clean the totals, rebuild every chart, and run a basic risk model. She had also added three practical recommendations.","This was not basic admin work. It looked like the kind of analysis consulting firms charged six figures to produce.","Alpha Killian looked up. \"This is normal for you?\"","\"On a slow morning.\"","The corner of his mouth almost moved.","Almost.","Then his expression turned serious again.","\"Marnie told me Beatrice Thorne recommended you.\"","Eira’s face gave nothing away.","\"You have a master’s in electrical engineering from Stanford and a connection to one of the best chip researchers in the country.\" He closed the laptop. \"But you took a placeholder job at Sterling Group.\"","He leaned back.","\"Why?\"","\"At the time, flexibility mattered more than the title.\"","It was a careful answer. Honest enough to sound reasonable. Vague enough to tell him almost nothing.","Alpha Killian stood and came around the desk.","\"Your husband runs Hale Group, one of our biggest competitors in tech. Then my aunt quietly places you inside my company.\"","His voice stayed calm, but his eyes remained fixed on hers.","\"You understand why that raises a few red flags.\"","\"You think Sebastian planted me here?\"","\"I think coincidences are usually just facts nobody has connected yet.\"","\"He didn’t.\" A bitter edge slipped into her voice. \"Sebastian has never thought I was capable of anything important enough to spy on.\"","Alpha Killian caught it.","\"So he underestimated you.\"","\"That makes two of you.\"","The words landed cleanly.","For a moment, neither of them spoke.","Then Eira added, \"Beatrice asked Marnie for a favor. Marnie helped me. That’s it. No master plan. No corporate espionage.\"","\"Maybe.\" Alpha Killian studied her. \"But it still doesn’t explain why no one knows Sebastian Hale has been married for four years.\"","Her expression cooled.","\"You’ll have to take that up with Sebastian.\"","\"You were okay with being kept a secret?\"","\"I wasn’t the one hiding the marriage.\"","That answer hit harder than it should have.","Eira picked up her laptop.","\"You have the reports. If we’re done here, I’m going to lunch.\"","She turned toward the door.","\"Miss Crawford.\"","Eira looked back.","Alpha Killian still had a hundred questions, but pushing harder would only make her shut down.","\"Nothing else,\" he said. \"Good work.\"","She gave him a short nod and walked out.","Alpha Killian stared at the closed door.","She had answered every question without giving him anything he could actually use.","For the first time in years, someone had walked out of his office still holding all the cards.","--","During lunch, Eira opened the shopping app on her cracked phone.","The newest model cost nearly eighteen hundred dollars.","Too expensive.","The thought came automatically. She had spent four years paying household bills and buying things for Alpha Sebastian’s family. Spending money on herself still felt wrong.","Then Alpha Sebastian texted.","Client dinner tonight. Be home on time. Don’t leave Serena alone. She’s still settling in.","Eira stared at the message.","Once, during her first visit to the Hale estate, Alpha Sebastian had refused to leave her alone.","She doesn’t know anyone here. I’m staying with her.","She had stretched that one kindness across four years of marriage.","Now he wanted her to offer the same kindness to his mistress.","Eira muted the conversation without replying.","Then she returned to the shopping app and chose the newest phone. Maximum storage. Same-day delivery to Sterling Tower.","She tapped Place Order, locked the cracked screen, and pushed the phone aside.","Her lunch had gone cold while she was shopping, and she had barely touched it.","When she reached for a drink, she remembered her water bottle was still at the lab.","She headed to the executive break room. It looked more like an airport lounge than an office kitchen.","A high-end coffee machine took up half the counter. The glass-front refrigerator held sparkling water, cold brew, and protein shakes. Baskets of protein bars and trail mix lined the shelves.","Eira opened the refrigerator and reached for a bottle of water.","A familiar mint scent reached her first.","Alpha Killian stepped beside her, took out the water, and handed it to her. Then he picked up a protein bar and set it beside her hand.","\"I only came in for water.\"","\"Your lunch is still sitting on your desk.\"","Eira looked up. \"Do you keep track of what every employee eats?\"","\"No.\"","The answer came a little too fast.","She glanced at the protein bar. \"Chocolate peanut butter.\"","\"It has protein.\"","\"It also tastes like drywall covered in frosting.\"","One dark eyebrow lifted. \"You’ve tried drywall?\"","\"Only on slow days.\"","His mouth almost curved. \"What do you like, then?\"","\"Food with an attitude.\" She twisted open the water. \"If it doesn’t fight back, I’m not interested.\"","\"So I picked wrong.\"","\"You didn’t ask.\"","\"No.\" His eyes stayed on hers for a beat. \"Next time, I will.\"","Then he walked out, leaving Eira with the water and the protein bar.","That morning, he had questioned her like a security risk.","Now he was remembering what she liked.","The man made no sense.","Worse, she was starting to pay attention.","By three, Eira had cleared everything on her desk.","That left her with one problem.","Going home.","She was still looking for an excuse to stay late when Natalie Brooks, one of the executive assistants, hurried over with a hand pressed to her temple. Her face had gone pale.","\"I’ve got a migraine, and I’m supposed to cover the Mercer dinner tonight.\"","\"I’ll take it,\" Eira said.","Natalie stared at her. \"You started this morning.\"","\"Send me the briefing.\"","\"It’s not just dinner. You’ll need the guest list, contract notes, meeting schedule, and car arrangements ready before anyone asks.\"","\"I can handle it.\"","Natalie studied her. \"You really want this assignment.\"","\"I really don’t want to go home.\"","Natalie’s expression softened. \"Fair enough. But Alpha Killian has to approve the switch.\"","Eira walked into Alpha Killian’s office.","He looked up from his laptop. \"What is it?\"","\"Alpha Killian, can I accompany you to tonight’s dinner?\"","\"You sure?\" Alpha Killian’s gaze was unreadable.","Eira nodded. \"I’m sure.\"","--","The Hawthorne was the kind of downtown steakhouse built for quiet deals and expense accounts.","When Eira entered the private dining room beside Alpha Killian, every man at the table stood to greet him.","One of them forgot to sit back down.","Alpha Sebastian.","His eyes locked on Eira, surprise giving way to suspicion.","Now she understood why Alpha Killian had asked if she was sure about coming.","Of course Alpha Sebastian was here.","He recovered a second too late and offered Alpha Killian his hand.","\"Alpha Killian.\"","Alpha Killian shook it once. His smile was polite, but his silver-gray eyes were not.","\"Problem, Hale?\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"Good. Then keep your eyes on the contract, not my assistant.\""]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14 Milk","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian took the seat at the head of the table. He glanced at Eira and tapped the chair beside his own.","\"Here.\"","Every eye in the room tracked the gesture.","\"New assistant, Alpha Killian?\" someone asked, fishing.","Alpha Sebastian’s stare drilled into them both. Mostly into Eira.","[She told me she quit. Now she’s riding shotgun for Killian Sterling?]","She had lied straight to his face.","\"Recently promoted from admin,\" Alpha Killian said, smooth as anything. He was clocking the tension between Alpha Sebastian and Eira with quiet interest.","Alpha Sebastian looked one bad comment away from cracking a molar. Eira sat there like the man was a stranger she’d been seated next to at a wedding.","Whatever was going on in that marriage, it was circling the drain.","Another guest jumped in. \"And your assistant’s name?\"","\"Eira Crawford,\" Alpha Sebastian answered before she could open her mouth.","The man raised his eyebrows. \"You two know each other?\"","Eira looked up. Honestly, she wanted to hear this one too.","\"We’re acquainted.\" Alpha Sebastian smiled. Thin. Polished.","Two words.","That was it.","Eira dropped her gaze, one corner of her mouth curling into something cold. Ten feet away, and the man still wouldn’t cop to the marriage in public.","Thank the Moon Goddess the divorce paperwork was already moving.","\"Is that right?\" Alpha Killian turned the question to her.","\"Yes, just acquainted,\" Eira said.","Alpha Killian’s silver eyes went a shade darker. \"Small world.\"","For the rest of the dinner, the table addressed her as Miss Crawford — and quietly did the math.","Anyone Alpha Killian parked at his right hand brought something to the table.","Not cute, not flashy, but the kind of cool, self-contained smarts that made people lower their voices without knowing why.","\"So that’s Alpha Killian’s type,\" someone murmured to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Knock it off. Miss Crawford is married.\"","\"And you know that how?\"","Alpha Sebastian had nothing.","\"That’s what I thought. You’re batting oh-for-two on straight answers tonight, buddy.\"","Alpha Sebastian didn’t bother replying. He drank again. For a guy who drank as much as he did, two glasses was basically water.","But Eira used to worry when he drank. Back home, two glasses in, she’d quietly swap his wine for water and slide a plate of food closer. No lecture. No fuss. Just done.","He was two glasses deep now. And she sat across the table working through her plate, calm and steady, without one glance his way. She wasn’t performing indifference — she genuinely did not care.","Something hot crawled up the back of his neck.","He set his glass down harder than he meant to.","Every head at the table turned.","Alpha Killian glanced up, unhurried. \"Is Sterling hosting the tech expo a problem for you, Hale?\"","\"Not at all.\" Alpha Sebastian drank half his glass in one go.","Alpha Killian waited until it touched the table.","\"I heard you were married, Hale.\"","Alpha Sebastian froze. His eyes snapped to Eira.","[Did she tell him?","No. She wouldn’t dare.]","One of the business partners laughed. \"That’s news to me. If Sebastian got married, we’d have heard about it — the man’s schedule is ninety percent work dinners. When would he even... OW.\"","He stopped mid-sentence. Alpha Sebastian had found his foot under the table.","\"Thanks for the interest,\" Alpha Sebastian said, smile tight. \"But my personal life isn’t worth the airtime. To the expo.\" He raised his glass.","Alpha Killian lifted his about an inch. The bare minimum.","\"There’s a networking gala after the expo,\" he added. \"Plus-ones expected.\"","A round of absolutely and wouldn’t miss it went around the table.","Glasses went up. Eira reached for her wine.","Alpha Sebastian’s face twitched.","He couldn’t stop himself.","\"Miss Crawford doesn’t drink.\"","The table went quiet.","Eira’s hand stopped halfway.","\"Better to get her something else,\" Alpha Sebastian went on, already waving down the server. \"Milk, maybe.\"","Milk.","A grown woman. At a contract dinner. In front of clients.","Someone coughed into a napkin. The Mercer partner suddenly found his bread plate fascinating.","The server kept a blank face and set a glass of milk in front of her.","Eira stared at it.","So Alpha Sebastian did remember things about her. Her tolerance. Her old habits.","He just used them the way he used everything about her. At the worst possible moment. For his own comfort. Without asking first.","She left the milk right where it was.","Then she picked up her wine and took a slow sip, eyes on no one.","Somewhere down the table, a laugh got smothered.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw locked. Cedar spiked into the air, sharp and sour.","Beside her, Alpha Killian’s mint stayed perfectly calm. He raised two fingers at the server.","\"She’ll have what I’m having.\"","The sommelier appeared with the bottle from Alpha Killian’s end of the table. The one that cost more than everyone’s entrées combined. He filled her glass.","Eira glanced over.","Alpha Killian was already reading the contract file again, like nothing had happened.","Dinner came out family style. A seared scallop platter sat at the far end, and Eira had been quietly tracking it all night. Every time it made it halfway down the table, it arrived empty.","She had given up on it.","Then the platter stopped right in front of her.","She looked up. Alpha Killian’s hand rested on the edge just long enough for her to serve herself. Then it was gone.","Five seconds, start to finish.","The whole exchange had been quiet enough that no one else caught it.","No one except Alpha Sebastian.","Across the table, he’d seen all of it. The wine. The scallops. The five seconds.","\"Excuse me.\" Alpha Sebastian stood abruptly. \"Restroom.\"","The second he cleared the room, he pulled out his phone and fired off a text.","[Outside. Now. We need to talk.]","Her battered phone lit up on the table.","Eira glanced at the screen and seriously considered leaving him on read.","Then the second message landed.","[Come out or I stop playing nice. Forget the one-month notice. I’ll walk back in there and tell Sterling you’re done. Tonight.]","Eira stared at the words.","[He’d do it, too. He’d spent the entire dinner refusing to claim her — but he’d burn the marriage as a weapon the second it got him what he wanted.","One ugly scene in front of Alpha Killian and the Mercer partners, and the job was finished. Her cover along with it.","No job meant no reason to leave the house every morning. Sebastian would want her home all day.","And at night, she’d be back to front-row seats for the Sebastian-and-Serena show.]","Her skin crawled just thinking about it.","She stood.","\"Excuse me, Alpha Killian. Restroom.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes flicked up. He gave a low hum of acknowledgment, but something in his face had gone cold.","Alpha Sebastian had walked out two minutes ago. He could do the math.","Eira didn’t have the bandwidth to worry about it.","The moment she stepped out of the private room, a hand clamped around her wrist and hauled her down the hallway.","\"Let go of me, Sebastian.\"","He didn’t. He steered her past the coat check and out a side door, into the dim corner by the valet stand. Only then did he let go.","Then he spun on her.","\"So this is you quitting, huh?\" His voice was low and boiling. \"You didn’t quit. You got a bump to the top floor. Nobody goes from pushing paper to the executive suite overnight. Nobody.\"","He stepped in closer.","\"So level with me, Eira. What else have you been keeping from me?\""]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15 Blind","paragraphs":["\"I did submit my resignation.\"","Eira stood in the wind by the valet stand, air pulling at a strand of her hair. Her eyes stayed level.","\"HR says one-month notice is standard. And the executive floor wasn’t my call. Take it up with Alpha Killian.\"","Alpha Sebastian searched her face for cracks. He found none.","\"Why would he pull you upstairs to play secretary?\"","\"No idea. Maybe he liked my typing speed.\"","\"Don’t get smart with me.\"","\"Then don’t ask questions you can’t handle the answers to.\"","Alpha Sebastian didn’t know much about Killian Sterling.","Sterling Pack sat too far above his ceiling. A man could grind his whole life and never touch the edge of Sterling’s coat.","What he did know: cold, sharp-tongued, kept women at arm’s length. Ruthless in business. Family got no free passes if the numbers didn’t add up. Other investors got decent returns. Alpha Killian got windfalls. At twenty-two, one high-stakes play had put Sterling Group knee-deep in emerging tech, and within two years it had become Hale Group’s biggest competitor.","Someone had once put it this way: Alpha Sebastian was the hardest-working kid in the room. Alpha Killian was born sitting at the table.","Effort was just the cover charge to meet genius.","So yes, Alpha Sebastian could work himself to the bone, and tonight was still the first time he’d ever shared a table with the man.","\"Eira, he’s twenty-eight and playing chess three moves ahead of everyone in that room. If he pulled you into his office, it’s not charity.\" His hands clamped down on her shoulders. \"Don’t tell yourself he sees talent. You don’t have anything he’d want. He’s probably just after—\"","He stopped himself.","\"Your face.\"","Eira looked at him for a long second.","Then she laughed. Short. Cold.","\"Wow. Four years of running your house, managing your Pack’s books, and cleaning up your sister’s messes — and the official appraisal comes back as my face.\"","She peeled his hands off her shoulders, one at a time. \"And hands off.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw worked. \"Alpha Killian’s a businessman. Businessmen chase profit. All his assistants are young and good-looking. Looks are a social tool.\" He locked eyes with her, dead serious. \"Quit. As soon as possible.\"","\"So your theory is I’m decoration.\" Eira crossed her arms. \"Funny. That’s the one job I already had. At your house.\"","\"Quit, Eira. Hand in the letter, pack your desk, go home. Done.\"","\"Home.\" Eira tilted her head. \"You mean the place where your acquaintance lives now? Hard pass.\"","His jaw went tight, fury simmering right under the skin. He couldn’t have explained why seeing Eira next to Alpha Killian had thrown him this badly.","So he filed it under the simplest label he had: she’s my wife. Mine. She doesn’t get to stand next to another man.","\"You’re my—\"","\"Your what?\" Eira cut in, voice flat. \"Say it. Out loud. You had a whole dinner table twenty minutes ago, and the best you managed was we’re acquainted. So whatever word you’re reaching for now, out here by the valet stand — save it.\"","\"This isn’t a debate. You’re quitting. That’s final—\"","\"That’s not your call.\"","Alpha Killian’s voice cut through the air.","He stood at the side door behind them, one shoulder against the frame. No telling how long he’d been there.","\"It’s mine,\" he said. Cool. Final.","His gaze slid over Alpha Sebastian like he was deciding whether the name was worth remembering.","\"And if you two are just acquainted, Hale, I’m not sure why you’re this invested in her career.\"","A pause. Then, with surgical precision:","\"That seems like her husband’s job. You know — the one who can’t buy his wife a working phone. The one living off her paycheck.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s neck went red.","He had nothing. And there was no version of tonight where he admitted he was that husband.","Alpha Killian’s eyes moved to Eira.","\"Long bathroom break, Miss Crawford.\" Flat. Businesslike. \"Let’s go.\"","\"Sorry. The line was terrible.\" She fell into step behind him without a backward glance.","The second she put distance between herself and Alpha Sebastian, her shoulders dropped half an inch.","Alpha Killian caught it.","Something complicated crossed his silver eyes.","\"So that’s why you volunteered tonight.\"","\"What?\" She glanced up, thrown for a second. Then it clicked. He’d figured out the marriage was done. She shrugged. \"Pretty much. Dinner with clients beats dinner theater at home.\"","\"How long?\"","No point hiding it now.","\"Four years.\" A beat. \"Four years and seventy-three days. But who’s counting.\"","Alpha Killian’s brow lifted. \"You, apparently.\"","\"Someone in that marriage had to keep records. He couldn’t even keep track of which woman lived in which room.\"","\"And in four years, he’s never once claimed you in public.\"","\"Not once.\" Eira looked straight ahead, chin up. \"His loss. I’m delightful.\"","--","Back inside, Eira had lost whatever appetite she’d had. The scallops were still on the table. She didn’t touch them.","Alpha Sebastian came back minutes later, hair damp at the temples, smile bolted back into place. He worked the room, glass in hand, toasting his way down the table.","When he got to Alpha Killian, he hesitated.","Alpha Killian didn’t lift his glass.","Everyone clocked it.","In their world, refusing a toast in front of witnesses was a public execution.","[Is he doing this over her?","Are they sleeping together?]","The second the thought landed, Alpha Sebastian’s face went dark. He drained his own glass in one go.","The dinner wrapped shortly after. Alpha Killian left first. Eira stood and followed.","Behind her, Alpha Sebastian slumped in his chair, half-drunk, phone already at his ear.","\"Serena.\"","One last needle. Smaller than it used to be.","[Fine,] Eira thought. [ Let’s speed this up.]","A drunk phone call wasn’t going to get an address across anyway.","She texted Serena Winthrop — the number was still on the welcome card Serena had pinned to the kitchen board, like she owned the place already.","[Sebastian’s drunk at the Hawthorne. Private room 3. Come get your prize.]","Send. Delete thread.","Outside, the night air cut through Eira’s coat. Alpha Killian’s car waited at the curb. The window lowered an inch.","\"You’re off the clock, Miss Crawford.\"","Then the window went up, and the car pulled away.","Three blocks later, Alpha Killian told the driver to circle back and park on a nearby side street.","Eira had attended the dinner on Sterling business. Making sure she had a ride home was basic risk management. At least, that was what he told himself.","From there, he still had a clear view of the Hawthorne’s entrance.","Eira tried to flag down a cab.","It drove right past her.","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened, but he stayed put. She would try again.","A while later, a black sedan pulled up. Serena hurried inside and came back with Alpha Sebastian leaning heavily against her. She helped him into the back seat and climbed in beside him.","The rear window lowered halfway as the sedan pulled from the curb.","Alpha Sebastian’s head fell against Serena’s shoulder.","Eira stood close enough to hear him mumble into her hair.","\"...Eira.\"","Serena went rigid.","Alpha Killian could not hear the word from where he sat. He only saw Alpha Sebastian folded against a woman who was not his wife, while Eira remained alone on the sidewalk.","That was enough.","The sedan disappeared into traffic.","Alpha Killian looked back at Eira as she shoved her hands into her coat pockets and started walking.","\"Bring the car around,\" he told the driver.","The Maybach pulled up behind her.","The window slid down. Alpha Killian sat inside, his face calm enough to suggest he had not spent the last ten minutes watching from half a block away.","\"Get in.\""]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16 Safe House","paragraphs":["Eira’s first instinct was to beg off. \"Alpha Killian, I appreciate it, but I can grab an Uber.\"","\"Your last cab blew right past you.\"","Fair point.","\"Get in.\" The door glided open. Not a request.","\"Thanks.\" Eira ducked inside. The second she settled in, she caught it — alcohol riding under the mint. Clean, top-shelf, but there.","He’d gone drink for drink with the whole table tonight and never so much as blinked. The man could hold his liquor, she’d give him that.","The driver glanced back. \"Miss Crawford, where to?\"","She almost gave her own apartment — the one across town, bought with her first research paycheck, sitting there with her life still packed in boxes. No sheets on the bed. Heat that took a day to wake up.","And an address she wasn’t handing out to anyone until the divorce cleared.","She course-corrected mid-breath.","\"Actually, scratch that. Just drop me at a hotel nearby. Whatever’s closest.\"","Alpha Killian’s mind went straight back to their first meeting. Hotel hallway. Half her face swollen purple.","\"He did that to you? Last time?\"","It took Eira a beat to catch up. Then she nodded.","Alpha Killian’s lip curled. \"All flash, no substance.\"","Eira kept her eyes down and let it slide. Silence settled in.","Then she noticed something.","The car kept cruising past hotel after hotel. The driver wasn’t even tapping the brakes.","She turned her head, tension creeping up her shoulders.","\"Where are we going?\"","\"You’ll see.\"","No specifics. Great.","Eira sat up straighter and pulled out her phone.","Alpha Killian caught the motion. \"What are you doing?\"","\"Sharing my live location with my lawyer.\" She didn’t look up. \"Standard procedure when a man says you’ll see instead of an address.\"","Alpha Killian stared at her for a second.","Then he turned to the window and decided the conversation wasn’t worth winning.","The corner of his mouth said otherwise.","--","The car pulled up in Palo Alto, outside a sleek mid-rise just off University Avenue. Eira knew this street. Back in grad school, she couldn’t have afforded the lobby.","\"Killian!\"","A girl in pink pajamas and bunny slippers came running out the door, waving both arms.","The window slid down.","\"Hi, gorgeous!\" Lila beamed at Eira. \"He texted me you were coming! I’m so pumped!\"","Eira looked from the grinning girl to the stone-faced man beside her.","\"So this is where you were taking me.\"","\"Lila. Take care of her.\"","\"On it!\" Lila looped her arm through Eira’s.","\"Good.\" One last glance at Eira. \"I’m out.\"","The Maybach pulled away without a sound.","Lila dragged her inside, practically skipping. \"Welcome to my palace! Eat anything, sleep anywhere. Or bunk with me. I’m a great cuddler.\"","Ever since this woman had caught her on the sidewalk and fixed her thesis in the same five minutes, Lila had been low-key obsessed. She’d spent all day wondering why the universe gave her a cold, unavailable brother instead of a smart, nice-smelling big sister.","\"I can sleep anywhere. Really.\"","\"Then you’re next to me!\" Lila pushed open a door. Soft blues. Crisp linens. \"Hate it? I’ve got two more rooms to pick from.\"","\"You decorated three guest rooms?\"","\"I get bored easily.\" She leaned against the doorframe, eyes going sly. \"Okay, real talk. My brother has never brought anyone here. Ever. So spill. How did you two actually meet?\"","\"Hotel elevator. I forgot to press my floor. He pressed it for me.\"","Lila’s jaw dropped. \"Shut up. You’re the one. The manager told me about a barefoot guest, slippers sent up, the whole—\"","She stopped herself. Physically bit her lip.","\"The whole what?\" Eira asked.","\"Nothing! Standard guest care. Five-star hotel stuff. Very normal.\" Lila grabbed a towel and a toothbrush and shoved them into Eira’s arms at escape velocity. \"Get some sleep! Sweet dreams!\"","The door shut a little too fast.","Eira stood there, towel in hand.","Slippers sent up.","So that night hadn’t been random hospitality. Someone had given an order.","Him. Obviously. It was his hotel — a distressed guest checks in barefoot, the owner flags it, staff handles it. Textbook liability management. Any decent CEO would do the same.","That was the reasonable explanation.","--","Down the hall, Lila whipped out her phone.","Lila: Why would you send her HERE?! Adults bond through PROXIMITY! This was your shot!","Killian: She was about to check into a random hotel alone at midnight.","Lila: So take her to YOUR place.","Killian: She’s my employee.","Lila: She’s also the first woman you’ve ever put in a car. Twice.","Killian: Stop projecting.","Lila: lol sure. Keep telling yourself that.","A voice message came through. Flat. Full of warning.","\"Not a word to Mom and Dad.\"","Lila rolled her eyes. Too late anyway. The manager had already leaked \"boss ordered VIP care for a mystery woman\" to the family the week before.","The group chat had lived off that scrap ever since. They just didn’t have a name.","Tonight, though? Hand-delivered to his sister’s apartment? That was brand-new material.","Another message landed.","\"Or you’re off the list for the tech mixer.\"","Lila’s face flipped in half a second. She typed in all caps.","Lila: OKAY OKAY LOVE YOU BEST BROTHER EVER NOT A WORD","That mixer was non-negotiable. One of the keynote speakers had trained under Dr. Alaric Thorne. That meant firsthand insight into sovereign processor work.","She had to be in that room.","--","Eira had just climbed into bed when her phone buzzed.","Beatrice Thorne.","Eira sat up before she even realized she’d moved.","Beatrice had been Dr. Alaric Thorne’s wife, and Eira had met her through him back at Stanford.","Somewhere along the way, Beatrice stopped being \"her advisor’s wife\" and started being the closest thing to a mother Eira had ever had, checking in on her too often, feeding her too much, worrying over her like it was her job.","She never understood the world Eira came from, the Packs, the bonds, the rigid hierarchy of Alphas and Omegas.","She picked up on the second ring.","\"Susan filled me in on the divorce,\" Beatrice said. No hello. Straight to business, same as always. \"Pack a bag. I’m picking you up tomorrow. You’re staying with me until the paperwork clears.\"","\"Beatrice—\"","\"Save it. I’m an old widow rattling around a big empty house, and my doctor keeps nagging me about living alone. You’d be doing me a favor.\" A beat. \"That’s our story, and we’re sticking to it. Even Sebastian can’t argue with a doctor’s note.\"","\"Thank you.\" Eira’s throat went tight. Just hearing that voice made her eyes sting.","\"Don’t be scared, kid.\" Beatrice’s voice shifted into that drill-sergeant-with-a-heart register only she could pull off. \"Alaric asked me to look out for you. But even if he hadn’t, I would. As long as I’m still kicking.\"","Eira exhaled. Some of the weight came off her chest.","\"One more thing,\" Beatrice went on. \"Tech expo next week. The invite landed on my desk. Skip the show floor. You’ve already seen everything they’re planning to brag about.\"","\"But the evening mixer? Worth your while. Young people, your field, real conversations. You’ve been buried in that lab way too long, and the results are going public soon. Time to come up for air.\"","\"The processor hits the market before long. You already know which companies will throw their hats in, but go put faces to the names. Call it fieldwork.\"","\"Conflict-of-interest rules keep you off the evaluation committee. Doesn’t matter. When push comes to shove, people will still want to know what the lead researcher thinks.\"","Eira heard what Beatrice was really saying under all of it: Get out there. Move on. You deserve better than what that marriage gave you.","\"I understand. I’ll go.\"","\"Good girl,\" Beatrice said, quieter now. \"Get some sleep.\"","The line went dead.","Eira set the phone on the nightstand and stared at the ceiling. The room smelled like lavender and fresh linen.","For the first time in longer than she could remember, she felt safe.","She was asleep before she could wonder why."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17 Aftermath","paragraphs":["Getting a two-hundred-pound drunk Alpha from the curb to his front door was not how Serena Winthrop had pictured her night ending.","Alpha Sebastian hung off her shoulder like a sandbag, reeking of expensive wine, mumbling to himself. She got him through the lobby, into the elevator, down the hall — sweating through a silk blouse that cost more than the doorman’s paycheck.","The things I do for you, she thought, jabbing the elevator button with her elbow. You’d better remember this.","He wouldn’t. He was too far gone.","She’d barely dropped him onto the couch when his hand caught her wrist.","\"Serena.\"","\"Serena Winthrop.\"","This time, he got the right name.","Her mood lifted a little. She sat down beside him. \"Oh, so now you know who I am. In the car, you called me something else.\"","The alcohol had fully taken over. Alpha Sebastian leaned his head on her shoulder, words running together. \"You are my wife.\"","Serena smiled, smug and satisfied. Then she pushed him back lightly, testing. \"No, I’m not. Eira is.\"","His brow creased, like the name took work to chew through. He said nothing.","\"Why did you marry her?\" she asked softly.","\"Wanted to marry you,\" he mumbled. \"But you left. You didn’t want me.\"","Her chest squeezed. She cupped his face in both hands. \"I told you I’d come back.\"","\"You left without telling me first.\"","\"That was my grandfather’s call. It happened fast.\" She kept her voice steady and patient. \"He sent me abroad for my career. He wouldn’t let me come back to see you. Still... thank you. For the funding, every month, all those years. It meant I never had to beg anyone.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s voice came out rough. \"Told you. Whatever I earn is yours.\"","\"Thank you, Sebastian.\" She leaned down and kissed him.","His pupils blew wide. He pulled her in and kissed her back.","Before long, they were tangled together on the couch.","--","The next morning, Alpha Sebastian woke with a splitting headache. He blinked at the ceiling, disoriented, and muttered the first thing that came to mind. \"God, my head. Get me some water.\"","\"Go back to sleep,\" a voice said beside him.","Not Eira’s voice.","Alpha Sebastian went stiff. He turned his head.","Serena’s face was inches from his, dead asleep.","He shot upright.","The movement woke her. She rubbed her eyes and pulled the blanket to her chest, sitting up too.","\"What’s wrong?\"","He swallowed hard. \"Did we — last night, did we—\"","\"Yeah.\" Serena nodded. \"You were wasted. I couldn’t exactly shove you off.\"","Alpha Sebastian swung his legs off the bed and dragged a hand down his face, like his brain physically couldn’t process the situation.","He’d slept with Serena. In the bed he shared with Eira.","\"I need a shower.\"","When he came out, Serena was already dressed. The hickeys on her neck were impossible to miss.","She looked at him, cheeks pink. \"You were... a lot, last night. Like you hadn’t touched anyone in years.\"","She stepped closer and wrapped her arms around him.","Alpha Sebastian looked down at this woman he’d been hung up on for years, and slowly returned the hug.","\"Eira and I never... we never did that.\"","\"I know.\" Serena held him tighter. \"I’ve always known you kept me in your heart, Sebastian. And I’ve only ever had you.\"","She tilted her head up and kissed the corner of his mouth.","For a moment, he smiled.","Then his expression froze.","\"Did Eira come home last night?\"","Serena’s face soured at the name. She held on tighter, like she was afraid he’d bolt.","\"No clue. Who even knows where she went.\"","Alpha Sebastian pulled away and walked into the living room. His phone sat on the counter, exactly where he’d tossed his keys. No missed calls. No texts.","His grip on the phone tightened until his knuckles went white.","\"Sebastian... are you worried about her?\"","\"Worried about her?\" His voice went flat, ice-cold. \"She can go wherever the hell she wants. It’s not like she’s got anywhere else in this city to run to.\"","\"Sebastian... do you have feelings for her?\" Serena’s voice cracked, eyes welling up.","His breath hitched. \"Don’t be ridiculous. I married her because she made a decent wife. That’s it. That’s the whole story.\"","He pulled Serena back into his arms.","She rested one hand over his heart. \"Would you ever... divorce her?\"","Alpha Sebastian hesitated.","Serena’s fingers curled slightly. \"Kidding. As long as you still care about me, that’s all that matters.\"","\"How could I not?\" He lifted her hand and kissed her knuckles. \"Just give me time to think about the divorce.\"","\"You know Eira’s situation. Fancy degree, no real job, can barely take care of herself. We’ve been married four years. I can’t just cut her loose overnight.\"","Serena’s gaze dimmed for a second. She forced a smile. \"I know you’re not that kind of guy. I won’t bring it up again.\"","\"You upset?\" His voice softened.","She shook her head. \"I’m the one who left first. Not exactly in a position to keep score.\"","\"Nobody’s keeping score.\" He glanced toward the kitchen. \"You hungry? I’ll cook something.\"","Serena nodded.","He opened the fridge and rooted around. Came up empty-handed.","Eira had always handled the groceries. She knew where everything was, what they were low on, when to restock.","Thinking about her made his jaw tighten.","\"Forget it. Let’s just grab breakfast out.\"","Serena wasn’t surprised. She looped her arm through his, all smiles. \"Works for me.\"","Downstairs, the elevator doors opened onto the lobby. A cab idled at the curb just outside the glass doors.","\"Serena... you should probably find your own place for a while.\"","Her smile slipped. \"You trying to get rid of me?\"","\"No.\" He shook his head. \"This building’s beneath you anyway. Let me put you up in a penthouse.\"","Serena’s face lit up like Christmas morning. \"Really? Thank you, Sebastian.\"","They walked right past the cab, arm in arm, heading toward the diner on the corner. Neither of them clocked the woman in the back seat.","Eira had only stopped by to grab a change of clothes.","It took less than five minutes to hear her almost-ex-husband promise another woman a penthouse."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18 Disgust","paragraphs":["A penthouse.","Alpha Sebastian had bought one for his parents, then another as a wedding gift for Isabella. Now he was offering a third to Serena Winthrop.","In four years, he had never offered his wife so much as a key in her own name.","Eira gave a short, bitter laugh.","She had only come back for clothes. Five minutes, in and out.","Then she opened the bedroom door.","Serena’s floral scent hung in the air, sweet and stale.","Eira shoved open a window. When she turned back, something black beneath the bed caught her eye.","A scrap of lace.","Not hers.","Her stomach tightened. She pulled back the comforter.","Rumpled sheets. Serena’s scent. More than enough evidence.","Alpha Sebastian and Serena had slept together.","In her bed.","\"Oh, God.\"","Nausea rushed up her throat. Eira barely reached the bathroom before she started retching over the sink.","It was not heartbreak.","It was disgust.","She rinsed her mouth, grabbed her bag, and left without the clothes she had come for. She could not stand another minute in that bedroom.","But the image followed her to Sterling Tower.","At her desk, she tried to drink some water. Black lace and twisted sheets flashed through her mind again.","Her stomach rolled.","She set the glass down and hurried to the executive restroom. Cold water. A locked door. Thirty seconds to get herself under control.","She gripped the sink and focused on breathing until the nausea passed.","Alpha Killian was always in before everyone else. He had seen her rush from her desk and followed a minute later.","He found Eira bent over the sink, still wearing yesterday’s clothes.","She lifted her head when he reached the doorway. Her face was pale. Her eyes were red.","Alpha Killian frowned.","Eira grabbed a paper towel and wiped her mouth. \"Alpha Killian.\"","\"Lila said you went home to change. \"His eyes moved over her once. Same blouse. Same skirt.","\"I ran out of time,\" Eira said.","\"Did you?\" Her gaze sharpened.","Alpha Killian leaned against the doorframe. \"Or did you find something that killed the plan?\"","He did not know the details. He did not need them.","Yesterday’s clothes. A trip home that lasted minutes. A husband he had seen leaving drunk with another woman.","The math was not hard.","Eira said nothing.","Something shifted in Alpha Killian’s face. He had meant to test the theory, not hit the nerve dead center.","\"You don’t have to tell me,\" he said.","\"I wasn’t planning to.\"","\"Good.\"","The answer came out colder than he intended.","He straightened, then set a sealed bottle of water on the counter beside her.","\"Take five minutes. If you’re still sick, you’re going home.\"","Eira stared at the bottle. \"That an order?\"","\"Company policy.\"","--","By the time the office filled up, a paper bag was waiting on Eira’s desk.","She looked up as Miles passed.","\"I didn’t order breakfast.\"","\"I know.\" He nodded toward the bag. \"Catering had an extra.\"","Inside was an egg sandwich, ginger tea, and a travel pack of antacids.","Eira checked the receipt. No name.","\"Catering keeps antacids on hand?\"","Miles adjusted his glasses. \"Apparently we’re very committed to employee wellness.\"","His face gave nothing away.","Technically, he had placed the order. The instructions had come from Alpha Killian.","\"Thanks,\" Eira said.","\"Of course.\"","A few minutes later, Natalie Brooks and Kate Morgan arrived.","Natalie dropped her purse beside her desk and looked at Eira. \"So? How bad was last night?\"","\"On a scale?\"","\"From free steak to three-hour hostage situation.\"","\"Somewhere in the middle.\"","Kate laughed as she set down her coffee. \"Sounds about right.\"","Natalie noticed the breakfast bag. \"Good. You’re eating. Did anyone pressure you to drink?\"","\"One client tried.\"","\"What happened?\"","\"Alpha Killian handled it.\"","Kate nodded. \"Yeah, he’s good about that. You say no once, and the conversation’s over.\"","Natalie sat down carefully. \"And seriously, thanks for covering for me. I barely made it home before that migraine knocked me flat.\"","\"No problem.\"","\"It was definitely a problem for me.\" Natalie opened her laptop. \"You saved me from smiling through dinner while my brain tried to escape through my eye socket.\"","A laugh slipped out of Eira.","Natalie pointed at her. \"There it is. I knew you could smile.\"","\"Don’t get used to it.\"","\"Too late.\"","The work itself was easy enough.","Calendars. Briefing packets. Last-minute travel changes. None of it came close to running a federal research team.","By late morning, Eira had cleared everything on her list and started reorganizing the next week’s schedule.","Kate glanced over from the next desk. \"You know you don’t get extra credit for making the rest of us look slow, right?\"","\"I’ll keep that in mind.\"","\"No, you won’t.\"","Natalie laughed without looking up from her laptop.","Before Eira could answer, Natalie’s phone buzzed. She checked the message and glanced toward Alpha Killian’s office.","A moment later, Miles stepped through the glass doors and handed her a black corporate card.","Natalie looked at it. \"Seriously?\"","\"Approved wardrobe budget for the tech expo,\" Miles said. \"This counts as paid work time. Stay under the limit and keep the receipts.\"","Kate was already reaching for her purse. \"Finally. A company policy I can support.\"","Eira looked between them. \"Wardrobe budget?\"","\"Sterling is hosting the expo next week,\" Natalie explained. \"Executive staff will work the show floor and the evening mixer. Press, investors, cameras. The whole circus.\"","Kate slipped on her coat. \"Translation: corporate doesn’t trust us to dress ourselves.\"","\"I’m very grateful. I’m also buying shoes.\"","Eira glanced toward Alpha Killian’s office. He was focused on his laptop, as if the shopping trip had nothing to do with him.","Natalie followed her gaze. \"You’re filling in on the executive team, so you’re included.\"","\"I already have clothes.\"","\"So did we,\" Kate said. \"Then the company offered to buy better ones.\"","Natalie picked up her purse.","\"Come on. We have an appointment.\"","Kate grinned. \"Let’s go make the corporate card nervous.\"","The company driver dropped them at Stanford Shopping Center, where the trees were trimmed, the storefronts gleamed, and even the parking lot looked expensive.","A personal stylist was waiting inside Nordstrom with a rack of event clothes already pulled.","Eira had walked through these stores with Alpha Sebastian once. He had promised to bring her back after Hale Group closed its next major deal.","The deal had closed.","The promise had disappeared.","Natalie led them toward the fitting rooms while Kate got distracted by a window display and walked straight into someone.","\"Watch where you’re going,\" a man snapped.","Eira stopped.","She knew that voice.","\"It’s fine, Sebastian,\" Serena said, soft and polished. \"It was an accident.\"","Kate stepped back. \"Sorry. I wasn’t looking.\"","Then she recognized him from industry events.","\"Alpha Hale?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s irritation disappeared behind his public smile.","\"Ms. Morgan. Good to see you.\"","Then his gaze moved past her and landed on Eira.","The smile froze."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19 The Confrontation","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian and Serena both stiffened when they saw Eira.","Serena slipped her arm from his—but not before Natalie clocked the luxury bags hanging from his other hand.","Natalie gave them a polished smile. \"Alpha Hale. And you must be Hale Pack’s Luna.\"","For half a second, Serena said nothing. Her smile stayed perfectly in place, but her eyes cut to Eira, waiting to see what she’d do.","\"No,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","He looked directly at Eira as he said it.","Serena’s fingers tightened around her purse strap before she recovered. \"Sebastian and I grew up together,\" she said lightly. \"He was just helping me pick out a few things for my new place.\"","Natalie and Kate exchanged a quick glance. They worked around powerful people for a living. They knew an explanation that arrived before anyone asked for one.","Serena turned to Eira, warm as spring. \"Eira. What a surprise. You walked right past us like we were strangers.\"","Eira looked at Alpha Sebastian.","He’d denied Serena was his Luna—but he still hadn’t said who actually held the title. Four years of marriage, and even now the truth was too inconvenient to say out loud.","\"I hope you’re not getting the wrong impression,\" Serena went on. \"This was just a quick shopping trip.\"","\"Of course.\" Eira’s gaze dropped, unhurried, to the designer bags in Alpha Sebastian’s hand. \"He’s always been very generous. With old friends.\" A beat. \"Some of them get penthouses. I got a resignation I have to work out.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","Serena’s smile flickered—just enough.","Natalie glanced between them. \"You know Alpha Hale?\"","\"We’ve met.\" Eira gave Alpha Sebastian exactly what he’d given her. Nothing more.","He should have been relieved. It was what he’d wanted for four years—no public claim, no awkward questions, no wife attached to his name. Instead, her flat calm got under his skin like a splinter.","Serena tried again, sweeter now, aiming for the audience. \"Are you two friends of Eira’s? That’s sweet. She doesn’t shop at places like this very often—you may need to walk her through it.\"","The insult came gift-wrapped.","Kate’s expression cooled.","But Eira answered before either of them could. \"You’d know, I’m sure. You’ve had a lot of practice lately—learning to shop on someone else’s card.\" She let her eyes drift, mild, to the bags in Alpha Sebastian’s hand, then back to Serena’s face. \"It shows. You wear it well.\"","Serena’s smile froze at the corners.","\"I only meant—\"","\"I know what you meant.\" Eira’s voice didn’t rise. It didn’t have to. \"You wanted these two to picture me lost in a boutique. Instead they’re wondering why a grown man is carrying another woman’s bags at ten in the morning.\" A pause, gentle as a blade laid flat. \"You should be careful what pictures you paint, Serena. People finish them.\"","For the first time, Serena had nothing polished ready.","Natalie stepped in, smooth, and linked her arm through Eira’s. \"She’s doing just fine. And she’s here with us.\"","Kate took Eira’s other arm. \"We have a fitting. Enjoy your morning.\"","They turned toward the fitting rooms.","\"Eira.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped forward and caught her wrist.","Eira stopped. She looked down at his hand, then up at him. \"Let go.\"","His grip tightened instead. \"We need to talk.\"","\"Then use your words, Alpha Hale.\"","The title put more distance between them than shouting ever could.","Natalie stepped forward. \"She said let go.\"","Shoppers had started to look. A woman near the display cases had already lifted her phone, angling it with the fake casualness of someone filming. Alpha Sebastian caught the movement—Alpha of Hale Pack, holding a woman by the wrist on a boutique floor. His grip loosened just enough for Eira to twist free.","\"This is private,\" he said, lower now.","\"Nothing about grabbing me in public is private.\" She nodded toward a quiet alcove near the fitting rooms. \"You have two minutes. They stay where they can see me.\"","She walked there on her own. Alpha Sebastian followed.","Natalie and Kate held position a few yards off, close enough to step in. Behind her shopping bag, Kate opened the Sterling executive chat.","Kate: Alpha Hale grabbed Miss Crawford on the floor. She got free but he’s pulled her aside. We still have eyes on her. Someone had a phone up. Want mall security?","At his desk, Miles read it.","Eira and Alpha Sebastian were still legally married. That gave Alpha Hale no right to grab her or pull her off a company assignment—and it didn’t make the situation any less volatile. He forwarded the message to Alpha Killian without a word of his own.","Inside Sterling Tower, Alpha Killian’s phone lit up.","He read the message once. Then he was already moving—phone to his ear, jacket left on the chair.","\"Lila.\" No greeting.","\"The boutique on the Sterling concourse. Now.\"","--","In the alcove, Eira folded her arms. \"You wanted two minutes. Start talking.\"","\"Why did you call me that?\" Alpha Sebastian demanded.","\"It’s business hours. You’re the Alpha of Hale Pack. I work for Sterling Group. What else would I call you?\" Her eyes stayed level. \"Last night I was only Miss Crawford to you. Funny how the title matters now that there’s an audience.\"","\"So that’s what this is about.\"","He reached for her shoulder. Eira stepped back before he could touch her. \"Keep your hands to yourself.\"","His jaw flexed. \"I wasn’t trying to hide our marriage.\"","\"No?\" Cool, even. \"You had a room full of witnesses and still couldn’t get the word wife past your teeth. She managed childhood friend three times. You managed nothing.\"","\"My position makes this complicated. I’m the CEO of Hale Group. You’re playing assistant to another man.\"","\"And somehow that embarrasses you more than carrying your mistress’s shopping bags in the middle of a mall.\"","\"She is not my mistress.\"","\"Right. You just buy all your childhood friends penthouses and let them sleep in your wife’s bed.\" She watched him. \"Tell me which part of that you’d like to say a little louder.\"","His face darkened. \"You know how people talk about CEOs and their assistants. I won’t have my wife turned into office gossip.\"","There it was. Not concern for her. Concern for how her job made him look.","\"So now I’m your wife.\" Eira almost smiled. \"You couldn’t say the word ten feet away, but back here, where no one can hear it, it comes out fine. That’s the whole marriage, Alpha Sebastian. In public I don’t exist. In private I’m supposed to obey.\"","\"I’m asking you to come home.\" His voice dropped. \"Quit Sterling. Stop this. We can start a family.\"","She stared at him. \"Now you want pups.\"","\"That was before.\"","\"Before what?\"","\"This is different.\"","\"What changed?\" She studied his face like a page she’d already read. \"Four years you told me you never wanted them. Not with me. Now Serena moves into my house and suddenly you want to be a father.\" A beat landed clean. \"Or is it that you need a Luna who’ll give Hale Pack an heir, and you’ve finally decided which of us is which?\"","A flash of panic crossed his eyes—there and gone. But she’d seen it.","\"Eira.\"","\"Don’t.\"","\"Don’t what?\"","\"Don’t say my name like you still have the right to.\"","For a second, neither spoke. Then his suspicion surfaced, uglier than before.","\"You didn’t come home last night. Where were you?\"","Eira almost laughed. The sheer nerve of it.","He had slept with Serena in their bed. And now he stood in a boutique alcove, jaw tight, demanding to know where she had spent the night.","\"Careful, Alpha Hale.\" Her voice went quiet—the quiet that ends things. \"You’re a man holding another woman’s shopping bags, asking his wife where she slept. Think about how that sentence sounds before you finish it.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s mouth opened. Closed.","For once, he had no idea which of them was supposed to be ashamed."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20 An Unexpected Alliance","paragraphs":["\"How do you know I didn’t go home last night?\" Eira asked, her eyes cold.","Alpha Sebastian studied her face, searching for some sign that she had seen him with Serena.","If she had walked into that bedroom, she would have cried. She would have confronted him. At least, the old Eira would have.","\"You didn’t,\" he said with sudden confidence.","\"I went back this morning. You were already gone.\"","Relief crossed his face before he could hide it.","Good. She had not caught them. No tears. No scene. No demand for divorce.","He noticed the red mark his fingers had left on her wrist.","\"Did I hurt you?\"","\"Yes.\"","He did not apologize.","\"Where were you last night?\"","\"With a friend.\"","\"Man or woman?\"","\"A woman.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Since when do you have friends?\"","Eira almost laughed. He knew so little about her that friendship sounded suspicious.","\"That’s none of your business.\"","\"Was it one of Sterling’s assistants?\" His mouth tightened. \"Stay away from them. People on the executive floor don’t do favors for free.\"","\"Who I spend time with is my choice.\"","Alpha Sebastian opened his mouth, but nothing came out.","A few yards away, Serena stood outside the boutique, pretending to study a window display while keeping one eye on them.","Eira turned to leave.","\"Eira!\"","Quick footsteps came down the corridor.","Lila hurried toward them in sneakers and a Stanford sweatshirt, slightly out of breath. She held up a faded hair tie.","\"You left this at my place.\"","Eira blinked. She had noticed it missing that morning but assumed it was gone for good.","\"You came all this way for a hair tie?\"","\"I was already on campus nearby.\" Lila gave the hair tie a small shake. \"It matches your bag, so I figured it might matter.\"","It had once. Alpha Sebastian had given it to her years ago.","Now it was only an old piece of fabric she had forgotten to throw away.","\"Thank you,\" Eira said.","The timing still felt almost too perfect. Eira made a mental note of it but said nothing.","Alpha Sebastian looked between them. \"You stayed at her place last night?\"","Lila finally turned to him.","\"And you are?\"","Before Eira could answer, Alpha Sebastian stepped in.","\"I’m her husband.\"","Lila went still. Then she looked him over from head to toe, making no effort to hide her disappointment.","\"You’re her husband?\"","The disbelief in her voice was impossible to miss.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression tightened. \"Is there a problem?\"","\"Technically,\" Eira said.","Alpha Sebastian turned to her. \"There’s nothing technical about it. We’re legally married.\"","\"Funny,\" Eira said. \"You had trouble remembering that last night.\"","His jaw locked. Cedar sharpened in the air before he pulled it back under control.","Lila looked between them and understood enough.","\"Got it,\" she said. \"One of those marriages.\"","\"Watch your tone,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","Lila lifted both hands. \"Hey, I’m just working with what you two gave me.\"","Alpha Sebastian studied her more closely. \"And you are?\"","\"Lila.\"","\"No last name?\"","\"Not one you need.\"","Her casual refusal to give him a last name irritated him.","Alpha Sebastian pulled out a business card and held it toward her, trying to take back control of the conversation.","\"Sebastian Hale. Thank you for looking after Eira last night.\"","Lila glanced at the card but did not take it.","Alpha Sebastian frowned at Lila, then looked at Eira as if to ask, This is the company you keep now?","Eira ignored him. She took the hair tie and slipped it into her pocket.","Lila was still slightly out of breath, so Eira handed her a tissue.","\"Thanks.\" Lila wiped her forehead, then glanced down at her Stanford sweatshirt and sweatpants. \"My brother called like the building was on fire. I didn’t even get time to change.\"","She linked her arm through Eira’s.","\"Come help me find something decent to wear.\"","\"Sure.\"","Eira turned back to Alpha Sebastian. \"Your two minutes are up.\"","She and Lila started toward the fitting rooms.","Alpha Sebastian called after her. \"Tomorrow is Isabella’s birthday. Pick up her gift and be home early.\"","Eira stopped and looked back.","\"I’ll send a gift.\"","\"That’s not enough. You still need to confirm the guest list, pick up the cake, and make sure everything’s ready before people arrive.\"","There it was.","Four years of birthdays, anniversaries, Pack dinners, and holiday parties. Eira had handled every invitation, every vendor, every last-minute disaster.","Then the Hale family had smiled for photographs and acted as if the evening had organized itself.","\"Isabella is your sister,\" Eira said evenly. \"Why are you giving me her birthday checklist?\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Because you’ve always handled these things.\"","\"Exactly. Your family relied on me for four years, then acted like I contributed nothing.\"","She took out her phone and forwarded him the guest list and contact details for the bakery, florist, and event decorator.","His phone buzzed.","\"There. You have everything.\" Eira slipped her phone back into her bag. \"From now on, the Hale family can manage its own events.\"","\"Eira, don’t start.\"","\"I’m not starting anything. I’m ending something.\" Her expression remained calm. \"Consider this my formal resignation as your family’s unpaid event planner.\"","She turned to leave, then paused.","\"One more thing. If tomorrow falls apart, don’t call me.\"","Eira met his eyes, her smile cool and faint.","\"Use the advice you gave me for four years.\"","\"Figure it out yourself.\"","She turned and kept walking.","Lila stayed quiet until they reached the next store.","\"Let me get this straight. He expected you to buy the gift, confirm the guest list, deal with the vendors, and clean up whatever went wrong?\"","\"That’s been the routine for four years.\"","\"And his contribution was what? Showing up?\"","\"Usually.\"","Lila stared at her. \"Wow. And I thought my brother was difficult.\"","Eira gave her a sideways look. \"Alpha Killian isn’t exactly easy.\"","\"No, but he knows assistants are employees, not unpaid family staff.\"","A laugh slipped out of Eira before she could stop it.","Lila brightened.","\"I’m serious,\" she continued. \"If my family threw a party, we’d hire people. We wouldn’t marry someone and quietly turn her into the entire operations department.\"","A beat. \"You know marriage isn’t a life sentence, right?\"","Eira looked at her.","\"People get divorced,\" Lila continued. \"They move on. Sometimes they upgrade.\"","\"Upgrade?\"","\"My brother, for example.\"","Eira stopped walking.","\"Does Alpha Killian know you’re trying to set him up with a married woman?\"","\"He knows I have excellent judgment.\" Lila’s grin faded into something more thoughtful. \"Honestly, though? I worry about him. He’s the strongest Alpha in the north. He runs everything, the Pack, the company, half the truce agreements between wolves and humans that keep this whole region from falling apart. Everyone needs something from him. Nobody just wants to sit with him.\"","\"That sounds lonely.\"","\"It is. And the worst part is the Moon Goddess hasn’t even bothered to fix it. Most Alphas his age have already found their fated mate by now. Killian’s twenty-eight and still nothing. No pull, no mark, no bond. Just him, alone at the top, waiting for a goddess who apparently forgot his name.\"","Eira said nothing.","\"But you,\" Lila said, tilting her head, studying her a little too closely, \"he doesn’t act like this around anyone. Not once, that I’ve seen. I’d bet money you two are fated.\"","Eira shook her head. \"That’s not possible.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Because I don’t have a wolf, no scent.\" Eira said it plainly. \"Wolfless Omegas don’t get fated mates. There’s nothing in us for the bond to catch on to.\"","Lila opened her mouth like she wanted to argue, then seemed to reconsider. \"Fine. No fated mate.\"","She brightened again, changing tracks entirely. \"But do you have any idea how good you actually are? That paper of mine, the one you fixed in like two minutes flat? It got approved. Clean pass, no more revisions.\"","Eira blinked, caught off guard, then let out a small laugh. \"So I take it you’re officially free from thesis hell?\"","\"Okay, don’t rub it in.\" Lila bumped her shoulder again, grinning. \"Point is, that’s not secretary work, Eira. That’s researcher work. Good researcher work. Whoever’s got you filing memos and confirming caterers is wasting a brain that clearly does better math than mine.\"","Eira thought of her hidden identity and only smiled, saying nothing.","A short distance behind them, Natalie and Kate stepped out from around the corner.","Kate lowered her phone.","\"Did Alpha Killian send Lila?\"","\"Had to,\" Natalie said.","Kate glanced back at Alpha Sebastian and Serena.","\"So Alpha Hale is Eira’s husband.\"","\"Apparently.\"","\"And the woman with him?\"","\"Definitely not his Luna.\"","Kate wrinkled her nose. \"Her scent is all over him.\"","Natalie looked at the luxury bags in Alpha Sebastian’s hand, then at Serena clinging to his arm.","\"He hides his Luna, takes another woman shopping, and still expects Eira to plan his sister’s birthday.\"","Kate shook her head. \"The nerve of that man.\""]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21 A Well-Deserved Slap","paragraphs":["Eira followed Lila to a designer boutique near the center of the mall.","Natalie and Kate trailed a few steps behind, still debating which store to visit next.","The glass doors were locked. A brass sign read:","BY APPOINTMENT ONLY","Lila pulled out her phone. One quick call, and the manager appeared less than thirty seconds later to unlock the door.","\"Miss Reed. Welcome back.\"","Eira glanced at Lila. \"Reed?\"","\"My mother’s family name,\" Lila said. \"I use it for private bookings. The Sterling name has a way of turning a quiet shopping trip into a full security operation.\"","The manager stepped aside. \"Right this way, Miss Reed.\"","Eira followed Lila inside.","The store was all cream carpet, soft lighting, and clothes without visible price tags. Voices drifted from a private fitting suite near the back.","\"Serena, what do you think?\" Isabella asked. \"Would this look good on me?\"","\"If it looks good on the model, it’ll look even better on you.\"","Eira stopped.","Serena.","Apparently, she had gone straight from breakfast with Alpha Sebastian to shopping with Isabella. She had even offered to buy Isabella a custom birthday dress.","With Alpha Sebastian’s money, no doubt.","Lila noticed Eira’s expression.","\"You know them?\"","Before Eira could answer, the manager lowered her voice.","\"Mrs. Hale and Miss Hale are in the adjoining suite.\"","Eira turned toward her.","\"Mrs. Hale?\"","\"Yes, ma’am. The appointment was booked under that name.\"","So Serena was already trying on the title in public.","Lila’s expression sharpened. She remembered Alpha Sebastian introducing himself as Eira’s husband less than an hour ago.","\"Wait. Is that his sister in there?\"","\"That’s Isabella.\"","Lila started toward the fitting suite.","Eira caught her arm.","\"Don’t.\"","\"Why not?\"","Eira glanced toward the closed door.","\"I want to hear how far they take this.\"","The fitting-room door swung open, and Isabella stepped out wearing a half-zipped designer dress.","\"Who’s out there? This was supposed to be a private appointment.\"","Then she saw Eira. Her face soured. \"What are you doing here?\"","Her gaze shifted to Lila’s Stanford sweatshirt and sweatpants. \"And apparently they’re letting anyone through the door now.\"","Lila blinked. \"Excuse me?\"","\"Watch your mouth, Isabella.\" Eira stepped between them.","Isabella laughed. \"You watch yours. Are you using my brother’s money to play rich again?\"","\"Isabella.\"","Serena appeared behind her in a cream silk dress, wearing concern like it had been professionally tailored.","She smiled at Eira.","\"We really do keep running into each other.\"","\"Mrs. Hale,\" Eira said evenly.","Both Isabella and Serena froze.","Serena recovered first.","\"There must’ve been a misunderstanding.\"","The manager said nothing. She knew exactly what name Serena had used when booking the appointment.","Isabella rolled her eyes. \"So what? Nobody would look at Eira and think she was Mrs. Hale. She’s basically a charity case.\"","Lila gave her a bright smile.","\"Wow. Designer dress, private fitting room, and still no manners. That’s rough.\"","Isabella stared at her. \"Excuse me?\"","\"I said money bought the dress.\" Lila’s smile disappeared. \"Shame it couldn’t fix the personality.\"","The Hale siblings had more in common than either of them realized. Neither one handled being challenged very well.","Serena studied Lila more carefully. The Stanford hoodie was oversized, but the watch at her wrist cost more than most cars. More important, the manager had unlocked the boutique for her without asking a single question.","\"Eira,\" Serena said, \"who is your friend?\"","\"She’s family,\" Lila answered, linking her arm through Eira’s.","Serena’s eyes narrowed. \"Family?\"","Isabella laughed.","\"What, another foster-care stray? Do they hand you people out in pairs?\"","Eira stepped between them.","\"I warned you about your mouth.\"","\"Or what?\" Isabella moved closer. \"You’ll cry to my brother again?\"","\"No.\"","Isabella reached out and shoved Lila’s shoulder.","Eira’s hand moved before anyone else could react.","The slap cracked through the boutique.","Isabella’s head snapped to the side.","The room went dead silent.","Eira lowered her hand.","\"That.\"","Isabella touched her cheek, stunned.","Then she lunged.","Two sales associates caught her before she could reach Eira. The manager immediately signaled the security guard stationed outside the boutique.","\"Miss Hale, step back.\"","\"Let go of me!\" Isabella twisted against them. \"She hit me! She’s nobody. My brother gave her a home, a name, everything!\"","Serena stepped forward, calm and polished, already slipping into the role of peacemaker.","\"Eira, this has gone far enough. Alpha Sebastian adores his sister. Apologize now, and I’ll explain everything to him.\"","Eira looked at her.","\"Mrs. Hale, I don’t need you doing damage control for me.\"","Serena’s expression hardened. \"Do you even hear yourself?\"","\"Loud and clear.\"","Eira turned to Lila.","Lila rubbed her shoulder. \"I’m fine.\"","Her eyes dropped for a moment.","\"I didn’t know you grew up in foster care.\"","Eira’s face stayed calm. \"Most people don’t.\"","\"I made some dumb comments earlier. About money. Families.\" Lila lowered her voice. \"If any of that landed wrong, I’m sorry.\"","\"It didn’t.\"","\"You sure?\"","\"I’m sure.\"","Lila looked back at Isabella, who was still fighting the store employees.","Then she grinned.","\"Also, that slap was incredible.\"","\"Who the hell are you?\" Isabella shouted. \"This has nothing to do with you!\"","\"You shoved me,\" Lila said. \"That made it my business.\"","\"I’ll have my brother make sure neither of you works in this city again!\"","Lila stared at her.","\"Oh no. A rich girl threatening to call her brother. Groundbreaking.\"","She pulled out her phone.","\"You’re not the only one with one.\"","Lila hit Call.","Alpha Killian answered on the first ring. \"What happened?\"","\"Someone shoved me at Stanford Shopping Center.\"","His voice changed immediately.","\"Are you hurt?\"","\"No. Eira handled it.\"","A brief silence followed.","\"Put the manager on.\"","At the same time, Isabella had Alpha Sebastian on speaker.","\"Sebastian! Eira hit me, and her crazy friend threatened me!\"","Alpha Sebastian’s voice cut through the phone.","\"Where are you?\"","\"The boutique at Stanford Shopping Center. Come get her away from me!\"","Lila raised her voice toward her own phone.","\"Also, they called Eira a foster-care charity case, and Isabella put her hands on me first.\"","The boutique manager closed her eyes for half a second.","Two powerful men on separate calls. Mall security on the way. One private appointment completely destroyed.","--","Alpha Sebastian was halfway to his next meeting when Isabella called.","He had the driver turn around.","By the time he reached the boutique, mall security was already there. Isabella stood near the fitting rooms with one cheek bright red, while Serena hovered beside her, calm and perfectly put together.","Eira and Lila waited across the store with Natalie and Kate.","The second Isabella saw her brother, she rushed toward him.","\"Sebastian, Eira hit me! In front of everyone!\"","Serena stepped in before he could respond.","\"Please don’t get angry. I’m sure Eira didn’t mean to. Things got out of hand.\"","It sounded like a defense.","It was not.","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze moved to Serena first. \"What are you still doing here? I told you to go home.\"","Isabella stared at him. \"Are you kidding me? She slapped me, and you’re asking Serena why she’s shopping?\"","Only then did Alpha Sebastian examine his sister’s cheek.","The mark was clear.","When he finally turned toward Eira, she was standing with her arms folded, calm enough to make him angrier.","\"Why did you hit Isabella?\""]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22 The Alpha Who Actually Showed Up 1","paragraphs":["\"Isabella has never respected me,\" Eira said, meeting Alpha Sebastian’s accusing stare. \"I used to let it go. Then she put her hands on my friend.\"","Lila stepped forward. \"I told your sister Eira was family. She called me another foster-care stray.\" Her voice sharpened on another. \"Meaning this wasn’t the first time she’d used that line on Eira.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze shifted to Isabella.","Lila was not finished. \"Then Isabella shoved me. Eira warned her once. Your sister decided to test the warning.\"","\"Sebastian, she’s twisting it!\" Isabella pointed at her red cheek. \"Eira hit me over one stupid comment.\"","\"You shoved her first,\" Eira said.","The boutique manager nodded. \"Security footage confirms Miss Hale made physical contact before Mrs. Hale responded.\"","The title landed hard.","Alpha Sebastian turned to Serena. \"You asked them to call you that?\"","Serena stepped forward. \"There’s been a misunderstanding. I used Sebastian’s client account, and the staff made an assumption.\"","The manager hesitated. \"The reservation specifically asked us to address you as Mrs. Hale.\"","Silence.","\"It was easier than explaining,\" Serena said softly. \"I didn’t think it mattered.\"","Eira almost laughed. Apparently, being his wife mattered only when Serena wanted the title.","Isabella cut in. \"Who cares? Eira is still an ungrateful charity case. My brother gave her everything.\"","Lila gave her an almost cheerful smile.","\"Quick question. Do you hear yourself when you talk, or is it just background noise in there?\"","Isabella glared at her. \"You think you’re funny?\"","\"No. I think you’re classist, cruel, and way too confident for someone currently losing an argument to security footage.\"","Eira covered a cough that sounded suspiciously like a laugh.","Isabella’s face went red.","\"Why are you defending her?\" she snapped. \"She wears cheap clothes, never bothers with makeup, and spent four years waiting on my family. What could you possibly see in her?\"","Lila’s smile disappeared.","\"I’m not trying to get anything from her. I like her.\"","The simple answer landed harder than an insult.","\"She’s smart. She’s kind. And she stepped in when you shoved me. Meanwhile, you’re standing in a private boutique insulting foster kids because your brother bought you a dress.\"","Isabella opened her mouth.","Lila held up one finger. \"Before you keep going, remember the cameras record sound too.\"","That shut her up.","Serena stepped between them, wearing concern like a second outfit.","\"Everyone’s upset. Isabella should apologize for what she said, and Eira should apologize for hitting her. Then we can put this behind us. I’ll explain everything to Sebastian.\"","Eira looked at her.","\"Mrs. Hale, I don’t need you handling my marriage, my apology, or my consequences.\"","Serena’s expression hardened. \"Do you hear how you sound?\"","\"Perfectly.\"","Alpha Sebastian turned to Eira. \"Get your friend under control.\"","Eira’s mouth curved slightly.","\"You’re not in a position to threaten her.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. He no longer recognized the woman standing in front of him.","Lila looked him over. \"So you’re Sebastian Hale. CEO of Hale Group.\"","She waited a beat.","\"Am I supposed to be impressed?\"","\"It should scare you,\" Isabella snapped. \"My brother can make one call and bury your career.\"","Lila glanced around the boutique. \"Hale Group wins a few contracts, and suddenly you think your family owns California. Adorable.\"","Isabella’s face darkened.","Eira stepped forward. \"Apologize to her.\"","\"Or what?\"","\"Or we let security footage, mall management, and your family’s lawyers decide what happens next.\"","\"Eira.\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice hardened. \"Stop threatening my sister.\"","\"She shoved Lila and insulted both of us.\"","\"Isabella lost her temper. You hit her.\"","\"And that makes everything she did disappear?\"","Serena touched Isabella’s arm. \"Just apologize. We don’t need to make this worse.\"","Isabella pulled away.","\"I’m not apologizing to either of them. If Serena were my brother’s wife, none of this —.\"","\"Isabella.\" Alpha Sebastian cut her off with one sharp look.","\"Apologize,\" Eira said again.","Isabella touched her burning cheek and stepped behind Alpha Sebastian. \"She hit me, and now I’m supposed to apologize?\"","\"Yes,\" Lila said. \"That’s usually what happens after you shove someone and insult them on camera.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped between them. \"Enough. Isabella shouldn’t have pushed you, but Eira crossed a line when she hit her. This ends now.\"","Lila stared at him. \"You always this good at blaming the person who fights back?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression cooled. \"This is a family matter.\"","\"No,\" Lila said. \"The second your sister shoved me, it became my matter.\"","Isabella gave a sharp laugh. \"You said you were calling your brother. Where is he? Did he chicken out?\"","Lila checked the time on her phone. \"He’s busy.\"","\"Sure he is.\"","Before Lila could answer, the boutique manager’s phone rang.","She listened for three seconds, then straightened.","\"Yes. Understood.\"","Two mall security officers appeared outside the locked glass doors. Behind them stood four men in dark suits, each wearing a small silver-wolf pin.","The manager’s face changed.","Sterling security.","The lead officer entered first. \"Miss Reed?\"","The boutique went silent.","Lila raised one hand. \"That’s me.\"","Isabella stared at her.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes narrowed.","Serena recovered first, but her grip tightened around her purse.","The manager looked down at the client profile on her tablet.","The private appointment had been booked under Lila Reed.","Reed had not meant much to her at first. There were plenty of Reeds in California.","But the Reed Pack in Washington, D.C., was something else entirely.","Old blood. Deep ties to the North American Pack Council. Senior members who traveled with trained Pack enforcers and enough political protection to make powerful Alphas think twice.","They were not simply wealthy.","They were protected.","The manager looked at Lila again.","Isabella glared at Eira and Lila.","\"Fine. Let’s take this outside and settle it.\"","\"There’s nothing to settle. \"The low voice came from the entrance.","Everyone turned.","Alpha Killian walked into the boutique with Miles behind him. Four Sterling enforcers remained outside the glass doors.","His silver-gray eyes swept over the room. Isabella’s red cheek. Serena standing beside Alpha Sebastian. Eira near Lila.","Then his gaze settled on the faint mark around Lila’s shoulder where Isabella had shoved her.","The air turned cold.","Lila’s face lit up. She caught Eira’s hand and pulled her closer.","\"Perfect. You’re here.\"","She pointed at Isabella.","\"She shoved me and called us foster-care strays.\"","Then she pointed at Serena.","\"She booked the appointment as Mrs. Hale.\"","Finally, she looked at Alpha Sebastian.","\"And he thinks this is all a family matter, so apparently none of it counts.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression changed.","Killian Sterling.","Miles stood behind him. Sterling security controlled the entrance.","The pieces clicked into place.","Lila Reed was Lila Sterling, Alpha Killian’s younger sister.","Serena recognized Alpha Killian immediately. She had once bragged about meeting him, and now the color drained from her face.","Isabella only saw another well-dressed Alpha entering with security.","\"Who are you?\" Isabella demanded.","\"Enough,\" Alpha Sebastian snapped. \"That’s Alpha Killian Sterling.\"","The name hit harder than Eira’s slap.","Isabella froze.","Sterling Pack sat at the top of the West Coast hierarchy. Hale Pack had only recently reached the second tier.","Her brother could threaten employees.","He could not threaten Alpha Killian Sterling’s sister.","The color drained from her face."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23 The Alpha Who Actually Showed Up 2","paragraphs":["Lila stepped forward. Isabella immediately moved closer to Alpha Sebastian.","\"You tried to scare me with the Hale name,\" Lila said. \"That might work on people who don’t know any better. It won’t work on me.\"","Her smile stayed pleasant.","\"And Eira is here on Sterling business. Put your hands on either of us again, and this stops being family drama. It becomes a legal problem.\"","Isabella took another step back and bumped into Serena. Serena pulled away on instinct, then quickly covered the reaction.","Alpha Sebastian was watching.","She could not afford to look annoyed with his sister, even if Isabella had just picked a fight with the worst possible people.","Alpha Sebastian caught Alpha Killian’s cold stare and turned to Isabella.","\"Apologize to Miss Sterling.\"","Isabella stepped out from behind him.","\"Miss Sterling, I’m sorry. I shouldn’t have called you a foster-care stray.\"","She tried to retreat again.","Lila raised an eyebrow. \"That’s it?\"","Isabella frowned.","\"You insulted Eira too,\" Lila said. \"Try again.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped in. \"What happens between Isabella and Eira is a family matter.\"","Alpha Killian’s gaze moved to him.","\"Family?\" he asked calmly. \"Last night, you said you and Miss Crawford were only acquainted.\"","Alpha Sebastian heard the mockery. Everyone else did too.","His jaw tightened.","\"Eira is my wife,\" he said. \"Isabella is my sister.\"","The boutique went quiet.","Serena’s fingers tightened around her purse.","For the first time in four years, Alpha Sebastian had publicly admitted the marriage.","Only because another Alpha had forced him to.","Alpha Killian looked at Eira. \"Is that true?\"","Her expression stayed calm.","\"Legally, yes.\"","Isabella’s mouth started to curve, but the movement pulled at her sore cheek.","Alpha Killian turned back to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Then your sister owes your wife an apology.\"","Alpha Sebastian studied him.","Alpha Killian had stepped in too quickly and too often for this to be simple professional courtesy. Alpha Sebastian recognized interest when he saw it, especially when it was aimed at his wife.","The idea made Alpha Sebastian’s blood run hot.","Eira had gone to Sterling Group to resign. Instead, she had landed on the executive floor and somehow gained Alpha Killian Sterling’s protection.","That was no coincidence.","Still, too many people were watching. Alpha Sebastian forced his anger down and softened his voice.","\"Eira. Do you really need an apology?\"","It was the tone he always used when he wanted her to make his life easier.","Lila opened her mouth.","Alpha Killian stopped her with a look.","The choice belonged to Eira.","She met Alpha Sebastian’s eyes.","\"Yes,\" she said. \"I do.\"","Isabella stared at her. \"You slapped me, and now I’m supposed to apologize?\"","Eira tilted her head. \"The security footage has audio. If you’ve forgotten what you said, they can play it back for you.\"","Isabella’s face froze. \"Sebastian!\"","\"We can discuss this at home,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"Not here.\"","\"Interesting,\" Eira replied. \"You suddenly care about keeping family matters private.\"","The words hit their mark.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened.","\"And I’m still working,\" Eira added. \"I’m not leaving.\"","\"You’re shopping,\" Isabella snapped. \"Don’t call that work.\"","Lila smiled. \"Good thing nobody asked you.\"","Alpha Killian glanced at Miles.","Miles stepped forward, tablet in hand.","\"Miss Crawford, Ms. Brooks, and Ms. Morgan are here on an approved company assignment,\" he said. \"Sterling Group is hosting the tech expo next week. Their event wardrobe is covered by the company.\"","He turned to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Miss Hale shoved Lila Sterling, insulted Miss Crawford, and threatened both women’s careers. The store has video and audio of the entire incident.\"","His tone remained professional.","\"Sterling Group needs a clear answer, Alpha Hale. Was your sister speaking for herself, or does Hale Group stand behind those threats?\"","Silence fell across the boutique.","Alpha Sebastian understood the trap immediately.","If he defended Isabella, he tied Hale Group to her threats. If he did not, she would face the footage, mall security, and Sterling Legal alone.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression hardened. Serena went pale.","Isabella looked from her brother to Miles, then toward the cameras.","\"Fine,\" she muttered. \"I’m sorry.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s voice sharpened.","\"Apologize to both of them. Properly.\"","Isabella’s face burned.","\"Miss Sterling, I’m sorry I shoved you and insulted you. Eira, I’m sorry for what I said about your background and your marriage. It was cruel and out of line.\"","Eira studied her.","\"I heard you.\"","Not forgiveness. Not acceptance.","Just confirmation that the apology had been made in front of witnesses and cameras.","Isabella exhaled, then muttered, \"You all act like I’m the only one who ever looked down on her.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze sharpened. \"Enough.\"","Isabella gave him a bitter look. \"Why? You think the same things. You just know how to say them without sounding rude.\"","Eira went still.","Isabella was not wrong.","Alpha Sebastian had spent four years dismissing her work, her education, and everything she had done for his family. His contempt had simply come dressed in better manners.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"I said enough.\"","Then he turned to Eira. \"What time are you done? I’ll pick you up.\"","\"No.\" The answer came so easily that he blinked.","\"Eira.\"","\"I already have plans.\"","\"Cancel them.\"","Eira gave him a cold look. \"That wasn’t a request for permission.\"","Serena’s nails pressed into her palms.","Lila looked between them, clearly ready to jump in, but Alpha Killian spoke first.","\"Miss Crawford is scheduled to review the expo briefing this afternoon.\" His tone stayed neutral. He did not order Eira to stay. He simply gave her an option.","Then his eyes moved to her. \"If she still wants the assignment.\"","Eira understood what he was doing. He was leaving the decision with her.","\"I do,\" she said. \"I’ll be back after the fitting.\"","\"Good.\"","Lila linked her arm through Eira’s.","\"I’ll ride back with her.\"","Alpha Killian glanced at his sister. \"You have lab work.\"","\"In the same building. I can manage.\"","\"That remains to be seen.\"","\"Rude.\"","Despite herself, Eira almost smiled.","Alpha Killian nodded toward the exit. \"Finish the fitting. Miles will have the briefing ready when you return.\"","\"Alpha Killian,\" Alpha Sebastian called.","Alpha Killian turned.","Alpha Sebastian chose his words carefully. \"Eira already submitted her resignation.\"","\"She did.\"","\"You can’t keep her employed against her will.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression did not change. \"Correct.\"","The simple agreement threw Alpha Sebastian off.","Alpha Killian continued:\"She can leave Sterling Group whenever she chooses. She also chose to complete her notice period and accept a temporary executive assignment.\"","His gaze moved briefly toward Eira, then back to Alpha Sebastian.","\"You seem to be the only man here confused about the word choice.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face darkened.","\"She’s my wife.\"","\"Then perhaps you should try speaking to her like a person instead of issuing instructions.\"","The words landed cleanly.","Alpha Sebastian looked toward Eira, but she had already reached the boutique entrance with Lila.","She did not turn around.","Alpha Killian waited until the doors closed behind her before facing Alpha Sebastian again.","\"Your marriage does not give you authority over her employment.\"","His voice remained calm. \"If you disagree, have your attorney call Sterling Legal. I’m sure they’ll enjoy explaining California labor law to you.\""]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24 The Wife Who Finally Fought Back","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian had not expected Alpha Killian to bring lawyers into the argument over one employee. The speed of it only deepened his suspicion.","\"What exactly is going on between you and Eira?\" he demanded. \"She’s married.\"","\"She works for me,\" Alpha Killian said. \"That’s all you need to know.\"","\"And if this isn’t only about work?\"","Alpha Killian’s expression never changed. \"Still none of your business.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped forward. Sterling security blocked him before he made it two feet.","Miles offered a calm, professional smile. \"I’d stop while you’re behind, Alpha Sebastian. Security has even less patience than Legal.\"","That did it.","\"Eira is my wife!\"","His voice carried through the boutique.","Serena went pale. Near the fitting rooms, Eira and Lila both stopped.","Four years of marriage, and Alpha Sebastian had finally admitted the truth in public. Not because he loved Eira. Not because he was proud to claim her. He had said it because another Alpha had challenged his authority.","It was not love.","It was ownership.","Alpha Killian left Alpha Sebastian standing there and crossed the boutique to Eira and Lila.","\"You both okay?\"","\"I’m fine,\" Lila said. \"Eira handled it.\"","His gaze shifted to Eira. \"I noticed.\"","Lila put her hands on her hips. \"Is that your way of saying she was wrong?\"","\"I’m saying next time, let security handle it.\"","\"Because hitting people is bad?\"","\"Because video evidence and lawyers hurt longer.\"","Lila considered that. \"Fair.\"","A faint smile touched Eira’s mouth.","\"Keep up,\" Alpha Killian said, already heading for the exit.","Lila linked her arm through Eira’s and followed.","\"How long have you been married?\" she asked.","\"Four years and a hundred fifteen days.\"","Alpha Killian glanced back.","She had given him the same exact number the night before. People did not count days unless they were waiting for something to end.","He said nothing.","Lila caught the look anyway.","\"What?\"","\"Nothing.\"","\"That was definitely not nothing.\"","Alpha Killian looked at his sister.","\"When you start dating, raise the bar.\"","Lila stared at him. \"I haven’t even been on one date. Why am I catching strays?\"","Eira lowered her eyes to hide a smile.","The warning had not really been meant for Lila.","--","Later, at a private urgent-care clinic, Isabella complained through the entire exam.","The physician had already confirmed that nothing was broken. Her cheek was swollen, her pride was worse, and she had demanded an X-ray anyway.","A nurse handed her a wrapped ice pack.","\"Twenty minutes on, twenty minutes off. Take ibuprofen with food.\"","Isabella pressed it to her face and winced. \"Sebastian, look at me. She could’ve broken my jaw.\"","\"She didn’t,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","His voice was flat enough to make her turn. \"Why did you bring up her foster-care background?\"","Isabella stared at him. \"Are you seriously defending her?\"","\"She didn’t choose how she grew up. Don’t use it against her again.\"","\"Sebastian,\" Serena said gently, \"Isabella’s in pain. This probably isn’t the time.\"","Isabella leaned toward her at once. \"See? Serena actually cares about me. Eira just hits people.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at the ice pack. \"She hit you once.\"","\"Once is enough!\" Isabella lowered the pack and glared at him. \"I’m your sister. Why do you keep taking Eira’s side? You love Serena anyway.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression went still.","\"I want Serena as your wife,\" Isabella continued. \"Everyone does.\"","Serena watched him carefully.","Alpha Sebastian looked away. \"Drop it.\"","Serena ’s face fell before she could hide it.","Then she recovered and gave Isabella a soft smile.","\"Your brother is married. Whatever happens next, he has to handle it the right way.\"","Alpha Sebastian thought about the night before.","Handle it the right way.","He was legally married to Eira and had slept with Serena in the bed he shared with his wife. There was no version of this that could be handled cleanly.","He turned toward Serena. \"I need time.\"","Serena’s expression softened. \"I’m not trying to corner you. You know I’ve always loved you.\"","She leaned into him.","After a brief hesitation, Alpha Sebastian put an arm around her.","Isabella watched them and quietly lifted her phone.","The photo she sent to the Hale family group chat showed Serena tucked against Alpha Sebastian’s chest while he held her close.","Luna Margaret responded first.","Finally.","Alpha Roger’s reply came a minute later.","[We need to discuss the legal and Pack consequences before anyone makes this public.]","Right after that, Isabella dropped a carefully angled selfie into the Hale family group chat, making sure her swollen cheek filled the frame.","Luna Margaret immediately called Isabella. \"What happened to your face?\"","\"Eira slapped me.\"","The satisfaction disappeared from Luna Margaret’s voice.","\"She did what?\"","\"She attacked me in the middle of a boutique. In front of everyone.\"","That was not quite what the security footage showed, but Isabella saw no reason to include the part where she had shoved Lila first.","Luna Margaret called Eira.","No answer.","She called again. Still nothing.","On the fourth attempt, the call went straight to voicemail.","Luna Margaret nearly dropped her phone.","\"She blocked me?\"","Eira had not blocked her. She had simply turned off the phone. The difference would not have mattered to Luna Margaret.","She called Alpha Sebastian next. \"Where is Eira?\"","\"She’s still working.\"","\"At this hour?\"","\"It’s not late.\"","\"That little office job is suddenly more important than this family?\"","Serena sat beside Isabella, helping her adjust the ice pack.","\"Aunt Margaret, Eira isn’t in the general office anymore,\" she said carefully. \"She was moved to Sterling Group’s executive floor.\"","Luna Margaret went silent. \"Doing what?\"","\"She’s filling in as Alpha Killian Sterling’s executive assistant.\"","Luna Margaret gave a sharp laugh. \"So she goes from a paper job to working directly for an unmated Alpha, and no one thinks that looks convenient?\"","\"Mom,\" Alpha Sebastian warned.","\"I’m asking a fair question.\"","\"Bring Eira home,\" Luna Margaret said over the phone. \"Before the entire Pack starts hearing rumors.\"","\"I’ll handle it.\"","Alpha Sebastian ended the call and set his phone facedown.","Serena lowered her eyes.","\"Alpha Killian is young,\" she said softly. \"And people notice him. If Eira keeps appearing beside him at dinners and public events, there may be talk.\"","The seed landed exactly where she intended.","Alpha Sebastian’s frown deepened.","Killian Sterling was younger than him, richer than him, and powerful enough to shut down a room without raising his voice.","Worse, he had looked at Eira as if she were worth studying.","He looked at her.","\"Do you think Killian Sterling is better than me?\""]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25 No Permission Needed","paragraphs":["Serena studied him for a moment. Then she smiled and brushed her thumb along his cheek.","\"Is that what’s eating at you?\" she asked softly. \"Maybe Eira thinks he is. I don’t.\"","She slipped her arms around his waist and rested her head against his chest.","\"You were the one who backed me when I left. You funded my research, covered my travel, and made sure I could focus on my career without answering to anyone.\"","\"I didn’t do that so you’d feel indebted to me.\" Alpha Sebastian gripped her shoulders. \"I did it because I believed in you. I wanted you to go as far as you could.\"","Serena looked up at him.","\"You gave me that chance.\" Her voice softened. \"And I never stopped loving you.\"","The words hit him harder than he expected. He had waited years to hear them.","Alpha Sebastian pulled her close.","Then his gaze drifted past her shoulder.","A leather briefcase sat on the entry table. Eira had given it to him after he became CEO of Hale Group.","Clients notice the details, she had told him. If you want them to take you seriously, walk in looking like you already belong at the table.","She had saved for months to buy it.","His arms loosened.","Serena noticed immediately. \"What’s wrong?\"","\"Nothing.\" He rubbed a hand over his face and stepped back.","\"The penthouse is already under contract. I’ll have a designer start this week.\"","Her face lit up. \"Seriously?\"","\"Yeah. Until it’s ready, I’ll put you in a serviced apartment nearby.\"","Her smile slipped. \"You want me out of here?\"","\"This place is complicated.\" He did not say Eira’s name. He did not have to.","Serena lowered her eyes. \"Right. Of course.\"","Alpha Sebastian lifted her chin. His gaze dropped to her mouth, but he kissed her forehead instead.","\"Give me some time. I’ll straighten everything out.\"","Serena nodded. But her mind was already moving.","If Alpha Sebastian had started hesitating, then Eira needed to leave before he had time to decide what that hesitation meant.","Serena had not come this far to lose him now.","--","Less than an hour later, Alpha Sebastian returned from dropping Serena at the serviced apartment.","A silver-haired man in a dark wool coat stood outside his door.","Alpha Sebastian recognized him from two academic fundraisers. \"Mr. Cole?\"","Martin Cole managed Beatrice Thorne’s household and personal affairs.","\"Mr. Hale.\" Martin gave him a polite nod. \"Mrs. Thorne asked me to let you know that Eira will be staying with her for a while.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Is Mrs. Thorne ill?\"","\"Nothing serious. She’s been having a difficult time since Dr. Thorne passed. Eira’s company would help.\"","\"I’ll bring Eira over in a few days.\"","\"That won’t be necessary.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"She’s my wife.\"","Martin’s expression never changed. \"She’s also an adult.\"","The words were polite. The message was not.","\"Mrs. Thorne isn’t asking for permission,\" Martin continued. \"She asked me to inform you so there wouldn’t be any confusion.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at him. \"Eira is still at work.\"","\"We’re aware. We’ll pick her up at Sterling Tower.\"","\"How long is she staying?\"","\"As long as Mrs. Thorne needs her.\" Martin paused. \"Or as long as Eira chooses.\"","Alpha Sebastian liked that answer even less. \"She’ll need to come home and pack.\"","\"Mrs. Thorne has already arranged anything she may need.\"","Another excuse gone before he could use it.","Martin gave him a final nod. \"Have a good evening, Mr. Hale.\"","He turned and walked back to the waiting town car.","Beatrice sat in the rear seat, wrapped in a charcoal cashmere coat.","\"Well?\" she asked as Martin got in.","\"He tried to stall.\"","Beatrice gave a dry laugh. \"He moves another woman into his wife’s home, but suddenly Eira spending a few nights with me is a bridge too far?\"","\"He said she was still at work.\"","\"Good. Saves us a stop.\"","Beatrice looked toward the driver. \"Sterling Tower.\"","The town car pulled away from the curb.","--","Eira had switched off her phone earlier, so she missed Beatrice’s calls.","\"Martin!\" She hurried toward him.","Martin smiled. \"Miss Crawford.\"","Eira had asked him more than once to call her Eira. He always agreed, then went right back to Miss Crawford. She had stopped fighting that battle years ago.","\"Mrs. Thorne is waiting in the car.\"","Eira looked through the open rear door. Beatrice was waiting inside.","\"Beatrice.\" The relief in Eira’s voice gave her away.","\"Give me one minute. I need to tell a friend I have a ride.\"","Eira walked back to Lila.","\"You’re officially off rescue duty. Beatrice came to pick me up.\"","Lila’s eyes lit up. \"Beatrice Thorne?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Can I meet her?\"","They approached the town car together.","\"Beatrice, this is Lila. My friend.\"","Beatrice’s face brightened. \"You made a friend.\"","Eira gave her a flat look. \"You don’t have to sound so surprised.\"","\"I’m not surprised. I’m thrilled.\"","Lila stepped forward and offered her hand.","\"It’s an honor to meet you, Professor Thorne. I’m Lila Sterling. I’m one of Professor Chase’s graduate students.\"","Beatrice shook her hand.","\"Professor Chase has mentioned you. He called you one of his strongest students.\"","Lila stared at her. \"He said something nice about me?\"","\"He did.\"","\"Wow. He usually saves compliments for published papers and dead scientists.\"","Beatrice laughed.","Lila spun toward the entrance. \"Killian! Get over here. Professor Chase apparently says nice things about me when I’m not around.\"","Alpha Killian stood near the doors with Miles. He had been watching Eira since the moment she saw Beatrice.","The guarded look she wore around everyone else had disappeared. Her shoulders had relaxed. Her whole face seemed lighter.","So this was what safety looked like on her.","He walked over. \"Professor Thorne.\"","Eira glanced between them. \"You know each other?\"","\"Barely,\" Alpha Killian said.","Beatrice turned serious.","\"Marnie told me you had questions about Eira’s placement. For the record, I asked her to arrange it. Hale Group had nothing to do with it.\"","\"I’ve already ruled that out.\"","\"Good.\"","\"But I still have a question.\"","\"Marnie told me Eira was your student. Her file also says she has a Stanford master’s in electrical engineering.\" His gaze settled on Beatrice.","\"With that background, she could have worked at a national lab or any major tech company in the country. Why hide her in a paper-only admin job?\""]}]);
